    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Flight-Record-Coordinator_R311892-1": {
      "title": "Flight Record Coordinator, Office of the Registrar",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity     Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University - Daytona Beach is seeking a detail-oriented and collaborative Flight Record Coordinator to serve as a vital link between the Office of the Registrar and the Daytona Beach and Prescott Flight Departments. Reporting to the University Registrar, this unique cross-functional role is responsible for ensuring the accurate exchange of data between academic and flight operations systems, maintaining regulatory compliance, communicating student status information to partner offices and supporting internal and external audits, record discrepancy review and resolution of record issues. The Coordinator will be responsible for ensuring appropriate messaging is departed to students through established communication channels. Additionally, this individual will maintain procedures, identify process gaps, and support improvements related to flight training records and academic records. The ideal candidate will be skilled in student data management, understand FAA, TSA, DOE and VA regulations as they pertain to flight training programs, and be experienced in higher education processes involving academic record management, satisfactory academic progress, registration, and scheduling. About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.  Qualifications Qualifications   Bachelor's Degree. A minimum of 1 to 3 years of relevant work experience is required. Type of work-related experience: Administrative/Compliance/Higher Ed/Flight Ops Strong knowledge of FAA, DOE, TSA and VA regulations and academic policies.  Excellent attention to detail, problem-solving skills, and organizational abilities.  Proficiency with student information systems (e.g., PeopleSoft) and flight scheduling (ETA) software.  Experience with Microsoft Access and Excel strongly desired To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311892 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Prescott-AZ/Marketing-Communications-Specialist_R312046": {
      "title": "Marketing Communications Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity:    As a Marketing Communications Specialist, you will play a crucial role in crafting compelling narratives for prospective students through innovative and impactful communication strategies. This entry level position offers an opportunity to blend creativity with strategic thinking, collaborating with internal stakeholders to shape the future of our marketing initiatives. Key Responsibilities: Collaborative Strategy Development: Engage in dynamic collaboration with internal stakeholders to formulate cutting-edge communication strategies. Interface seamlessly with digital, social media, and creative services teams to drive cohesive cross-team initiatives. Needs Assessment and Goal Establishment: Proactively identify communication needs and establish strategic goals in partnership with internal stakeholders. Assess the viability of requests, ensuring alignment with overarching marketing objectives. Resourceful Print and Digital Management: Liaise with marketing team members when requests necessitate print or digital resources. Collaborate closely with the Digital Communication Specialist to craft compelling email copy and gather email assets. Independent Storytelling: Independently source captivating success stories from students, faculty, and alumni. Craft engaging written materials such as blog posts, newsletters, and articles, determining the optimal distribution channels for maximum impact. Organization and Maintenance: Uphold and manage degree-specific playbooks, content databases, communication flows, and other material repositories. Ensure efficient organization and accessibility of materials to support streamlined communication processes Adaptive Responsibilities: Embrace a dynamic work environment with the readiness to undertake various assigned duties to contribute to the overall success of the team and organization About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.         Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Qualifications   ​ Education: Bachelor's degree in Communications, Marketing, or a related field. Experience: Proven track record in marketing and communications, showcasing successful strategies. Technical Skills: Proficient in Microsoft Applications with expertise in leveraging them for effective communication. Familiarity with Salesforce and Marketing Cloud. Demonstrated writing and editing skills for crafting polished content. Multichannel Expertise: Experience in print, email, digital, and social media platforms. Strategic Decision-Making: Ability to make editorial decisions aligning with recruitment lifecycles, university policies, and goals. Interpersonal Skills: Excellent interpersonal skills for effective collaboration with diverse stakeholders. Innovative Thinking: Innovative thinker with the ability to challenge existing methods. Work Style: Independent worker and self-starter, thriving in both autonomous and collaborative environments. Organizational Skills: Highly organized, deadline-oriented, and a skilled communicator with a strong grasp of writing principles. Motivation: Self-motivated with the ability to seek guidance when necessary.   To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R312046. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
