    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Grounds-Supervisor_R308738": {
      "title": "Grounds Supervisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Opportunity:  The Grounds Supervisor is responsible for the effective management of all landscaping and grounds maintenance activities. This role requires expertise in irrigation systems, pest control for turf and ornamentals, and disease identification in plants. The supervisor will also handle material ordering, scheduling, and at times perform hands-on tasks alongside the team. A key aspect of this role includes testing irrigation systems and conducting yearly evaluations for staff. The successful candidate will be required to obtain an LLO pesticide license within the first 90 days of employment. Key Responsibilities: Team Leadership and Supervision: Supervise and mentor grounds maintenance staff, providing guidance and support to enhance skills and efficiency. Conduct annual performance evaluations for team members, identifying areas for improvement and professional development. Landscaping and Maintenance: Oversee the maintenance and enhancement of landscaped areas, ensuring adherence to quality and design specifications. Participate in hands-on maintenance tasks when necessary to demonstrate best practices. Irrigation Management: Design, install, and maintain irrigation systems, ensuring efficient water usage and optimal plant health. Regularly test and evaluate irrigation systems for functionality and efficiency. Pest Control and Disease Management: Identify pests and diseases affecting turf and ornamental plants, implementing integrated pest management strategies. Develop treatment plans for pest control and disease management in compliance with regulations. Material Ordering and Inventory Management: Order necessary landscape supplies, including plants, herbicides, fertilizers, and equipment. Manage inventory levels to ensure all required materials are available for maintenance tasks. Scheduling and Project Management: Create and manage work schedules for grounds maintenance staff to ensure timely completion of tasks. Prioritize and assign daily activities based on project needs and environmental conditions. Record Keeping and Reporting: Maintain accurate records of maintenance activities, pest control applications, and inventory management. Prepare reports on grounds maintenance operations for management review. Safety and Compliance: Ensure all operations comply with safety regulations and industry standards. Conduct safety training sessions and promote a culture of safety among team members. About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Generous Time Off :   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions :   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.      Compensation     The hourly range for this role is   up to  $20.00 . The final offer will be based on the candidate’s skills, qualifications, and experience, as well as applicable state regulations, internal equity, and business needs, and may fall outside of the stated range.   Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent; degree in horticulture, landscape management, or related field preferred. Minimum of 5 years in grounds maintenance or landscaping, with at least 3 years in a supervisory role Required licenses, certificates, and/or security clearances: Obtain an LLO pesticide license within the first 90 days of employment, ensuring compliance with state and local regulations. Relevant certifications in pesticide application and irrigation management preferred. Candidates will be expected to obtain a Limited Lawn and Ornamental Pesticide License (LLO) by the State of Florida within the first 90 days of employment. We are excited to share that Embry-Riddle will cover the cost for the Grounds Supervisor to obtain a Limited Lawn and Ornamental License. Must possess and maintain a valid, US driver’s license. Must meet the University’s standards for approved drivers. Unacceptable driving records (as stated in the Use of Equipment and Vehicles Procedure 1.17) include the following (for three years from the date of each occurrence): Three (3) or more at-fault accidents and/or moving violations in the previous 36 months. Two (2) or more at-fault accidents or two (2) or more moving violations in the past year. Conviction for driving while impaired (DWl, DUl within the last five (5) years). Conviction for death by vehicle, hit and run, racing, careless and reckless driving, implied consent in the previous five (5) years. Serious violations result in immediate disqualification and revocation of driver privileges. The following are examples of serious violations ​ : Speeding over 15 mph of the posted limit, driving under the Influence of alcohol or drugs, leaving the scene of an accident, reckless or careless driving, Use of vehicle in (drug trafficking, reckless homicide, soliciting), unlawful use of weapons, driving under suspension or revocation, fleeing a police officer, vehicle theft, Improper or illegal lane change, following too close, and passing a stopped school bus while stop sign is engaged. Required knowledge, skills, and abilities: Comprehensive understanding of landscaping practices, turf management, and ornamental horticulture. Proficient in irrigation systems design, maintenance, and testing. Familiarity with pest control methods and plant disease identification. Strong leadership and team management abilities. Excellent organizational and scheduling skills. Proficient in computer applications for scheduling, record keeping, and inventory management. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Detail-oriented with a commitment to high-quality standards. Working Conditions: Ability to work outdoors in various weather conditions. Physical ability to lift and carry equipment up to 50 pounds. Flexibility to work occasional weekends and holidays as needed. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R308738. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Prescott-AZ/Academic-Advisor_R312021": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity       Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University (ERAU) seeks a dynamic, student-centered, and forward-thinking Academic Advisor to provide visionary leadership   The Academic Advisor for Undergraduate Students at Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University, Prescott Campus, provides comprehensive academic guidance and student support within a rigorous, aviation and STEM focused learning environment. This role supports students from matriculation through graduation by assisting with academic planning, course selection, degree requirements, university policies, and institutional resources. Advisors work closely with faculty, student services, and campus partners to promote student success, retention, and timely degree completion while upholding Embry-Riddle’s academic standards and mission. The advisor serves as a primary point of contact for undergraduate students, offering individualized advising that aligns academic goals with career aspirations in aviation, aerospace, engineering, security, and related fields. Responsibilities include monitoring academic progress, interpreting degree audits, supporting students on academic probation or at risk, and providing guidance on registration, transfer credit, internships, and experiential learning opportunities. The position also contributes to orientation programs, outreach initiatives, and campus events, and maintains accurate advising records in compliance with university and accreditation requirements. This role requires strong knowledge of Embry-Riddle Prescott academic programs, excellent communication skills, and the ability to support a diverse student population in a fast paced, mission driven campus environment. Primary Job Functions, Duties, or Accountabilities: Foundations of Academic Advising Assist students with registration, course selection, academic planning, schedule adjustments, and other program updates. Refer students to appropriate university resources when questions arise. Engage with the advising team for cross training Enforce university policies and procedures, ensuring students understand degree requirements, transfer credit policies, and the importance of co-curricular engagement.  Collaborate with faculty and other stakeholders to track student progress, identify at-risk students, and provide timely outreach. Work with specified cohorts based off of your committee codes.  Ensure clear communication with fellow advisors by informing them of any interactions or work conducted with their assigned students. Uphold strict confidentiality and ethical advising practices.  Advisors must stay within their designated scope of responsibility and avoid involvement in decision-making outside their role.  Professional Responsibilities & Campus Engagement Attend all required department meetings, training sessions, and professional development opportunities in person. Participate in committees and campus initiatives as assigned. Actively contribute to UNIV101 workshops. Serve as a liaison to other departments (Admissions, Registrar, Housing, etc.), ensuring clear and appropriate communication. Accurately maintain student records using university-approved technology and systems. Support & Outreach Assist in planning, organizing, and executing university-wide events such as New Student Orientation, Open House, and Spring Preview Day. Represent the advising team at events, fostering connections with prospective and current students, parents, and campus partners. Ensure that event participation aligns with the department’s mission and objectives. Student Outreach & Retention Strategies Conduct targeted outreach to first-year students and students identified as academically at-risk. Implement proactive strategies to engage and support students in achieving academic success. Maintain detailed documentation of outreach efforts and follow-up actions. Collaborate with relevant campus colleges and departments to ensure a coordinated approach to student success. About us   For nearly 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.     Today, our faculty, researchers and professiona l staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.     Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle! Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.  Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.  Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.       Compensation   The annual salary range for this role is   up to  $ 46,000. The final offer will be based on the candidate’s skills, qualifications, and experience, as well as applicable state regulations, internal equity, and business needs, and may fall outside of the stated range.   Qualifications Bachelor's Degree in STEM subject, psychology, sociology, counseling, communication, education or other related field 1-3 of experience in Student Support or Administrative   To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311806. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Full CV   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.     Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .        Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/San-Diego-California/Assistant-Professor-of-the-Practice-of-Applied-Aerospace-Science--Remote---US-_R311655": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of the Practice of Applied Aerospace Science (Oceanside, CA)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity The College of Aviation (COA) at Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University Worldwide (ERAU-W) is seeking an Assistant Professor of the Practice of Applied Aerospace Science. A requirement of this position is to teach 9-week cohorts of transitioning military members 18 semester hours of aviation maintenance courses. The position will require conducting face-to-face classes, 8 hours per day at the ERAU WW Oceanside campus, CA, with an approximate a 10-week break between cohorts. As an additional requirement, the successful candidate must remain current in the needs and requirements of the aviation maintenance industry to provide cohort students mentorship that would lead to successful employment. About the College of Aviation The mission of the College of Aviation is to develop and provide graduate and undergraduate academic programs that enable students to excel in the multi-disciplinary field of aerospace; in the aeronautics industry, in the military, and in the local, state and federal government organizations connected to aerospace programs. The mission also includes assessing program outcomes and using these assessments to update courses and programs. About us For nearly 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries. Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow. Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace. Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle!    Generous Time Off: Enjoy 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year’s Day. Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26. Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period. Qualifications Required Education and Qualifications: Candidates must have an earned Master’s Degree and a Federal Aviation Administration Airframe and Powerplant Certificate. A background in providing military technical training is desired, but not required. The candidate must also have a strong desire to assist transitioning military members into successful civil aviation maintenance careers. Application process/requirements Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R311655. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: Cover letter Full CV Statement of teaching philosophy Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process) Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday. Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website . Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
