    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Research-and-Instruction-Librarian_R311970-1": {
      "title": "Research and Instruction Librarian",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity     The Hunt Library at Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University (ERAU) invites applications for the position of Research and Instruction Librarian serving a diverse population of residential and online students. The Research and Instruction Services Department is currently hiring for a Research and Instruction Librarian who is passionate about serving students through research consultations and instruction, developing information literacy, and engaging in creative partnerships with faculty through liaison relationships. The successful candidate will join the Hunt Library https://huntlibrary.erau.edu/, serving Daytona Beach and our Worldwide Campus of online students, working regular business hours including nights and weekends. This professional staff position reports to the Associate Director for Research and Instruction Services. Hunt Library is a forward-thinking, technologically advanced library organization on the Ex Libris ALMA ILS and offering a robust range of electronic collections and integrated library software. Duties include working as part of a team providing reference services in-person, virtual, and electronic modes, developing online learning objects, sharing in synchronous and asynchronous library instruction, and participating in collaborative team and cross-departmental assignments and special projects. No aviation or aerospace background is required: we welcome librarians from a wide variety of academic disciplines who will enjoy working with our dedicated, hardworking students. Growing the research presence and agenda is at the heart of the ERAU strategic plan, and Hunt Library provides an excellent opportunity for librarians who want to engage with the development of research skills among undergraduate and graduate students. Consider joining our team. Recent graduates and mid-career librarians are encouraged to apply. A leader in the provision of higher education in the fields of aviation and aerospace, ERAU offers regionally accredited bachelors’, masters’, and doctoral degrees. For more information on ERAU, see http://www.erau.edu/about/index.html . For more information on the Hunt Library, go to http://huntlibrary.erau.edu/about/ . Information on the new library facility is available at https://studentunion.erau.edu/. About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.         Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Qualifications The Hunt Library values diversity, equity, and inclusion and is committed to hiring staff who share these values. We strive to create a collegial, inclusive culture of belonging for our staff and students, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds. Required Qualifications: · ALA-accredited master’s degree in library science or information studies. · Library reference and research assistance experience, or an interest in research librarianship as a career path. · Library instruction experience and/or an interest in developing pedagogical skills in librarianship. · Demonstrated ability to learn new technology tools and skills and remain current with emerging technologies and processes. · Demonstrated ability to work independently and collaboratively with a diverse population of faculty/staff, students, and colleagues. · Ability to work collaboratively across library and organizational teams for projects such as collection management, promotion of library resources, and development of new library artifacts and initiatives. · Excellent analytical, interpersonal, time management, organizational and problem-solving skills. · Excellent written and oral communication skills. · Experience communicating effectively in a virtual environment. Preferred Qualifications: · Academic library experience. · Instruction or training experience and comfortable presenting to small and large groups. · Database knowledge and searching proficiency. · Experience developing online learning objects or online modules. · Experience training, supervising, or mentoring student assistants. · Experience developing, providing, or assisting with events. · Proficiency with learning management software such as Canvas. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311970. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Prescott-AZ/Director-of-Facilities_R311978": {
      "title": "Director of Facilities",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity       Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University is seeking an experienced and strategic Director of Facilities to lead day-to-day facilities operations for the Prescott, Arizona campus. Reporting to the Vice President for Facilities, this position provides leadership across facilities maintenance, utilities, transportation, shipping and receiving, grounds, housing maintenance, and project management. This is a highly visible leadership opportunity for a facilities professional who can balance day-to-day operational needs with long-term planning and campus priorities. The Director will work independently to evaluate facility needs, develop solutions, manage resources, oversee contractors and projects, and contribute to the continued development of the campus facilities master plan and standard operating procedures. The ideal candidate will bring strong facilities or construction leadership experience, sound judgment, financial and project management skills, and the ability to lead teams across multiple trades and service areas. This position also serves as a member of the Prescott Chancellor’s Campus Leadership Team and is an on-call role responsible for responding to after-hours facilities issues. Key Responsibilities Lead, supervise, coach, and evaluate facilities personnel across multiple trades and service areas, including electrical, plumbing, HVAC, energy management, grounds, transportation, building services, materials management, and housing maintenance. Plan, schedule, and oversee maintenance activities and external contractors to ensure campus buildings, grounds, utilities, mechanical and electrical systems, and safety and security systems are properly maintained. Develop, implement, and oversee preventative maintenance, renovation, and facilities improvement programs. Contribute to the development and maintenance of the campus facilities master plan and standard operating procedures. Evaluate current and future facility needs and provide recommendations and options to support strategic campus planning. Oversee fleet vehicle maintenance, transportation services, shipping and receiving, and event setup activities. Manage grounds and landscape operations, including irrigation, fertilization, pesticide applications, and seasonal snow removal. Oversee housekeeping contract requirements and ensure campus facilities and grounds are maintained to an aesthetically pleasing standard. Manage physical plant and construction projects from planning through completion, including developing specifications, estimating costs, preparing bid specifications, and coordinating contracted services. Oversee outside contractors and ensure projects are completed in accordance with specifications, applicable requirements, and established timelines. Coordinate with code officials regarding required permits and inspections. Collaborate with the Design and Space Planner, Information Technology, and Planning and Construction teams on campus projects and furniture, fixtures, and equipment (FF&E). Manage significant operational and capital expenses while ensuring responsible use of resources. Participate in the Prescott Chancellor’s Campus Leadership Team and provide facilities expertise to campus leadership. Respond to after-hours facilities issues as required in this on-call position. About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.       Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.      Qualifications Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Engineering or a related field . Five or more years of progressively responsible experience in physical plant maintenance, facilities, construction, or engineering. Three or more years of supervisory experience, or a combination of education and experience commensurate with the requirements of the position. Demonstrated knowledge of facilities management and/or auxiliary services principles and practices. Knowledge of construction rules, regulations, and compliance requirements. Knowledge of RFP and bidding processes, as well as contractual terms and conditions. Ability to read, analyze, and interpret construction drawings and specifications. Ability to interpret financial reports and legal documents. Demonstrated ability to negotiate contract terms. Strong supervisory and leadership skills. Ability to exercise independent judgment, make decisions, and resolve problems with limited supervision. Preferred Qualifications Experience leading facilities operations in a complex campus, institutional, higher education, or similarly diverse environment. Experience managing multiple facilities trades and service functions simultaneously. Experience overseeing large-scale construction, renovation, or capital improvement projects. Experience managing contractors, consultants, and competitive bidding processes. Experience with strategic facilities planning, preventative maintenance programs, and long-term capital planning. Strong communication, negotiation, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Work Environment This position is based on the Prescott campus and requires the ability to work across indoor and outdoor environments and respond to facilities needs as necessary. The position is on call at all hours of the day , with minimal travel required. The position description notes exposure to changing weather conditions, confined spaces, and hazardous materials. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311978. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Industry-Expert-Research-Scientist--Center-for-Aerospace-Resilient-Systems--CARS---Daytona-Beach-Campus_R311844-1": {
      "title": "Industry Expert Research Scientist, Center for Aerospace Resilient Systems (CARS), Daytona Beach Campus",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nVariable time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity The Center for Aerospace Resilient Systems (CARS) is seeking globally recognized aerospace systems industry technical leadership experts to help strengthen and grow the CARS research portfolio, with a near-term focus on aerospace cybersecurity, AI, Quantum computing, CNS ATM / C5ISR research in the civil and defense aerospace, and space systems domains. These research positions will lead the acquisition and support the execution of high-quality research, contributing to advancing knowledge in enhancing aviation and aerospace resilient systems. CARS is seeking self-motivated leaders who collaborate effectively across industry and government stakeholders, and engage with faculty, staff, and students to pursue innovative research projects and contribute to the overall mission of the Center. All projects are focused on student-engaged research to fund PhD, Master's, and undergraduate student research activities. The Center’s mission is to be a world leader in the research and innovation of safe, secure, and resilient aerospace system solutions that meet the needs of our global aerospace community. Strong research-focused candidates eager to proactively identify and address key aviation and aerospace systems resiliency challenges are encouraged to apply. This position is funded through the researcher's externally secured research activities, and is designed for individuals, including retirees from industry or major institutions, who continue to conduct research through ERAU/CARS and independently secure grant funding to support their work while serving as Principal Investigator. Individuals may also serve as personnel supported by grants led by other CARS investigators. Position Levels: Depending on preparation and experience, the position can be set at various levels, including Research Scientist and Senior Research Scientist. These positions provide diverse opportunities for individuals at different career stages to become part of a dynamic team and contribute to CARS research initiatives in aviation and aerospace resilient systems. Research Scientist Serves as an independent scientific researcher or a collaborator on a multi-scientist research initiative and may have lead responsibility for discrete components of a larger project under the general direction of a senior or principal investigator and is expected to capture and lead research proposals that can significantly aid in a research center’s ongoing projects. Requires a minimum of 20 years of relevant industry experience. While a Ph.D. (or equivalent terminal degree in a relevant discipline) is valuable, leadership and innovation in industry-government/industry technology development and research are most important. Candidates must have a demonstrated record of research engagement, including the influence, capture and/or execution of relevant new technology development or research projects. Senior Research Scientist An accomplished and experienced professional researcher who conducts significant original research or serves as a senior collaborator on a multi-scientist research initiative, typically leading substantive aspects of the overall project under the general guidance of a principal researcher. A Senior Research Scientist is expected to capture and lead large-dollar-value research proposals that can significantly aid in a research center’s ongoing projects and may serve as a co-investigator and / or principal investigator of externally funded research grants. Requires a minimum of 30 years of relevant industry experience. While a Ph.D. (or equivalent terminal degree in a relevant discipline) is valuable, leadership and innovation in government/industry technology development and research are most important. Candidates must have a demonstrated record of research engagement, including the influence, capture, and/or execution of relevant new technology development or research projects. A Senior Research Scientist is expected to capture and lead large-dollar-value research proposals (greater than $1M/yr) that can significantly aid in a research center’s ongoing projects and may serve as a co-investigator and / or principal investigator of externally funded research grants. About the Embry-Riddle Center for Aerospace Resilient Systems: ERAU's Center for Aerospace Resilient Systems (CARS) is the Embry-Riddle research center dedicated to advancing aviation and aerospace resilient systems, focusing on highly connected aerospace systems & operations including cybersecurity, AI, integrated systems, and rapid prototyping, supporting commercial and defense industries. CARS is committed to collaborating with industry and government partners, providing innovative solutions to pressing resilience challenges. The Center's work spans a broad spectrum of systems-related domains such as: aviation & aerospace cybersecurity including cutting-edge tools for enhancing cybersecurity in the operational technology (OT) domains, artificial intelligence / machine learning (AI / ML) and data science / data analytics, software engineering, , Communications / Navigation / Surveillance Air Traffic Management (CNS ATM) and Command / Control / Communications / Computing / Cyber / Surveillance / Reconnaissance (C5ISR) technologies and systems, human-machine interfaces, virtual and augmented reality training systems,  airspace/airport modeling & simulation, including  civil and defense airspace systems.  The Center also maintains a vast historical Air Traffic database (archived since 1999).  CARS has a support staff in place to assist with proposal development and project management. CARS is at the forefront of driving resilient systems innovation to foster a safe, secure, and resilient future of the aviation and aerospace ecosystem. About us For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries. Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow. Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace. Qualifications Applicants with the following expertise are encouraged to apply: Candidate must have or be able to acquire a US security clearance. Aviation and Aerospace Systems Expertise in any of the following areas: Aviation / Aerospace cybersecurity domain knowledge Comprehensive knowledge of aviation and aerospace systems, operations, principles, regulations, and best practices. Understanding of cybersecurity risk assessment, vulnerability management, systems resiliency evaluation, and testing within the aerospace domain. Application of AI/ML and Quantum computing. Leadership and Collaboration Skills Demonstrated ability to foster collaboration among industry, government, and academic leaders.  Ability to work with and mentor students in CARS research efforts. Proven track record of bringing diverse stakeholders together to achieve common goals. Research Proficiency: Demonstrated background in research and data analysis. Experience in designing and conducting aviation and aerospace systems research. Innovation and Thought Leadership: Ability to promote and support innovation in aviation systems through new technologies, strategies, and practices. Demonstrated thought leadership in aviation and aerospace systems. Ethical and Professional Standards: Commitment to integrity, ethical conduct, and adherence to professional standards in aerospace systems-related work. Communication and Networking: Excellent communication skills to effectively convey aerospace systems concepts, research findings, and ideas to diverse audiences. Strong networking skills for building working-together relationships. Regulatory / Compliance and Systems Standards Knowledge: Familiarity with aviation and aerospace systems standards at the global and regional levels. Interdisciplinary Collaboration: Ability to work across disciplines to address resilience challenges, incorporating insights from engineering, human factors, policy, and other relevant fields. Data Analysis and Decision-Making: Strong analytical skills for interpreting systems data and making data-driven decisions to enhance resilience measures. Continuous Improvement Mindset: Willingness to adapt and improve strategies based on emerging trends, technologies, and lessons learned. Adherence to Core Values: Commitment to upholding the core values of integrity, innovation, and collaboration in all endeavors. Global Perspective: Awareness of and adaptability to the global nature of the aviation and aerospace ecosystem, considering diverse regulatory environments and cultural factors. Candidates possessing a diverse range of these expertise areas will be well-prepared to effectively contribute to the realization of CARS's vision, mission, and objectives aimed at advancing aviation and aerospace systems resilience. Additionally, candidates must demonstrate proficiency in generating financially viable and pertinent research proposals, followed by effective project execution upon securing contracts. A forward-looking perspective on the aviation and aerospace systems industry, coupled with strong verbal and written communication skills, is imperative. The capacity to thrive in industry, government, and academic environments is mandatory. Supervision and project management, conducted in a collaborative yet results-driven manner, are pivotal for long-term success.  Successful candidates for this role are individuals with a proven history of autonomously initiating and executing research outside of established research centers. Application process/requirements To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R311844 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: Cover letter Full CV Research Statement Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process) Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday. Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website .  Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Academic-Records-Specialist_R311388": {
      "title": "Academic Records Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Embry-Riddle: Celebrating 100 Years of Leadership in Aviation and Aerospace     As Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University marks its Centennial, we proudly celebrate 100 years of advancing the future of flight and aerospace education. With vibrant residential campuses in Daytona Beach, FL, and Prescott, AZ — and a Worldwide network spanning nearly 120 global locations — Embry-Riddle stands as the world’s largest aviation and aerospace university.     For a century, we have led innovation in STEM education, serving more than 30,000 students around the globe. Our cutting-edge programs in Applied Science, Aviation, Business, Technology, Engineering, Safety, Security, and Space empower the next generation of leaders to shape the future of flight, exploration, and discovery.     As we launch our next century, we remain committed to excellence, innovation, and preparing graduates who will transform industries and redefine what is possible.   The Opportunity   The Office of the Registrar at Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University offers a collaborative and student-focused environment that values innovation, operational excellence, and a commitment to student success. As part of this dynamic team, you will play a key role in supporting the academic mission of one of the world’s leading universities in aviation and aerospace education. This position provides an opportunity for a motivated professional to develop administrative expertise, strengthen student records management skills, and grow their career within a high-performing academic services environment. Team members are committed to delivering high-quality service to students, faculty, staff, and external stakeholders while supporting one another in a fast-paced and mission-driven setting. Key Responsibilities Student Records & Processing Process student record actions including registration, record updates, academic adjustments, and credit assignments Maintain and update student records within the Student Information System Research archived records and recreate missing information to produce official transcripts Apply transcript notations, academic standing updates, and other academic record entries Process National Student Clearinghouse updates as required Transcript Services Review, process, and deliver electronic and paper transcript requests using Parchment system software Determine eligibility for transcript release in accordance with FERPA and university policy Maintain and track pending transcript requests and ensure timely follow-up Communicate ineligibility or account issues with students and campus partners Customer Service & Communication Provide daily support to students, advisors, and stakeholders via phone and email regarding transcripts and records Deliver professional, accurate, and timely responses to inquiries Interface with federal, state, and local agencies requesting student educational records Validate requests and ensure compliance with FERPA and institutional policies Coordinate subpoena requests and required documentation with appropriate university offices Administrative Support Provide administrative assistance to committees and departmental initiatives as needed Collaborate with campus partners to maintain accurate historical academic records Support continuous improvement of records processes and service delivery     Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle!   Health Benefits:   Experience comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, along with wellness programs that include preventive care and fitness memberships. Our flexible spending and health savings accounts simplify managing healthcare costs. Join a workplace that prioritizes your health—because your journey to wellness should be rewarding! Buckle up for a healthier, happier you!   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.     Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes an annual 6% gift of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution, with no vesting period.   Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.         Compensation   The hourly rate for this position is up to $17.15 . The final offer will consider the candidate’s skills, qualifications, and experience, along with applicable state regulations, internal equity, and business needs, and may fall outside of the stated range.       Qualifications Education: Associate’s degree preferred Area of Concentration: Business Administration, Office Administration, Higher Education, or related field preferred Experience: 1–3 years of clerical or customer service experience required Experience in administrative support, records management, student services, or related office environment preferred Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities: Strong knowledge of State, Federal, and University policies, including FERPA compliance Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, Microsoft Teams, student information systems, and third-party software applications Strong organizational, analytical, research, and problem-solving skills Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced, detail-oriented environment Strong written and verbal communication and customer service skills Ability to contribute to a positive, collaborative, and team-oriented work environment Self-motivated with strong attention to detail and sound judgment in handling sensitive information Licenses, Certifications, and Security Clearances: None required Application process/requirements   To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number   R31138 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Full Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Prescott-AZ/Associate-Director--Flight-Department_R311943": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Flight Department",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity The Associate Director (AD) of the Flight Department provides operational leadership and administrative oversight for the University's flight training program. The AD assists the Director in managing the daily operations of the department, ensuring safe, efficient, and effective flight training while supporting the University's mission of academic excellence, student success, regulatory compliance, and industry engagement. The AD serves as a key member of the Flight Department leadership team and acts on behalf of the Director as assigned. Responsibilities include supervision of flight instructors and staff, oversight of scheduling and resource utilization, coordination with academic and operational departments, and implementation of departmental strategic initiatives. Essential Duties and Responsibilities   Department Administration Assist the Director in the daily management and administration of the Flight Department. Provide leadership and supervision for assigned operational and administrative personnel. Serve as acting Director in the Director's absence. Assist in developing, implementing, and evaluating departmental policies, procedures, and operational standards. Participate in department, college, and university committees as assigned. Perform additional duties as assigned by the Director.   Flight and Maintenance Operations Oversee the day-to-day operation of flight training and aircraft maintenance activities. Ensure compliance with all applicable FAA regulations, university policies, accreditation standards, and safety management system (SMS) requirements. Coordinate aircraft utilization, instructor staffing, and scheduling to maximize operational efficiency. Monitor operational performance and implement continuous improvement initiatives. Assist in emergency response planning and operational risk management.   Personnel Leadership Assist with recruiting, onboarding, mentoring, scheduling, and evaluating flight instructors, maintenance personnel and administrative staff. Foster a professional culture emphasizing safety, customer service, collaboration, and continuous improvement. Coordinate professional development opportunities for department personnel. Support performance management and corrective action processes when necessary.   Student Success Assist in implementing and supervising student advising processes related to flight training progression. Monitor student performance, retention, and completion metrics. Collaborate with academic advisors, faculty, and student services to support student success. Address student concerns and facilitate timely resolution of operational issues.   Academic Support Collaborate with academic leadership to align flight training with degree program requirements. Assist in scheduling courses, assigning instructors, and maintaining instructional records. Support curriculum implementation and continuous program assessment. Participate in accreditation activities and program reviews as required.   Budget and Resource Management Assist in preparing and administering departmental operating budgets. Monitor expenditures and recommend efficient use of university resources. Coordinate equipment, aircraft, simulator, and facility utilization. Support long-range planning for fleet, technology, and facility improvements.   Regulatory Compliance and Safety Promote and maintain a strong culture of aviation safety. Ensure compliance with FAA Part 141 requirements and applicable federal, state, and university regulations. Support internal audits, inspections, and accreditation reviews. Maintain required operational documentation and records.   External Relations Develop and maintain relationships with industry partners, government agencies, and aviation organizations. Represent the department at university events, recruiting activities, conferences, and professional meetings. Support internship, employment, and partnership initiatives benefiting students and the department.   About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Aviation, Aviation Management, Aeronautical Science, or a closely related field. FAA Commercial Pilot Certificate with Airplane Single-Engine Land and Multi-Engine Land ratings. FAA Certified Flight Instructor (CFI) certificate. Minimum five years of progressively responsible experience in collegiate or professional flight training. Minimum three years of supervisory or management experience. Demonstrated knowledge of FAA Part 141 flight training operations. Excellent organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced operational environment.   Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in Aviation, Education, Business Administration, or related discipline. FAA Certified Flight Instructor–Instrument (CFII) and Multi-Engine Instructor (MEI). Experience managing university flight operations. Experience with Safety Management Systems (SMS). Experience with accreditation and regulatory compliance. Budget management experience. Experience using flight scheduling and training management software (e.g., Flight Schedule Pro, Talon, ETA, or similar).   To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311943. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Full CV   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Assistant-Director-of-Electronic-Resources-Management_R311841": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Electronic Resources Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University (ERAU) invites applications for the position of Assistant Director of Electronic Resources Management to join the Hunt Library. This position provides strategic oversight of the library's electronic resources program, supporting the teaching, learning, and research mission of Embry-Riddle's Daytona Beach, Prescott, and Worldwide campuses. Reporting to the Senior Associate Director for Collection Strategy & Technical Services, the Assistant Director of Electronic Resources Management leads the planning, acquisition, licensing, assessment, and lifecycle management of the library's electronic resources. The position manages more than $2 million in annual electronic resource expenditures, supervises the Access & Discovery Librarian, and collaborates with colleagues across the Hunt and Hazy Libraries to ensure seamless, sustainable access to electronic resources. The successful candidate will join the Hunt Library ( https://huntlibrary.erau.edu ) on the Daytona Beach campus working regular business hours. Hunt Library is committed to fostering an inclusive, equitable workplace and a collegial culture of belonging for our employees and students. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds. Primary Responsibilities Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Provide strategic leadership for the planning, acquisition, licensing, implementation, assessment, renewal, and lifecycle management of the library's electronic resources. Manage the library's electronic resources budget, currently exceeding $2 million annually, including budget monitoring, financial analysis, expenditure tracking, and long-term planning. Negotiate electronic resource licenses and vendor agreements while maintaining productive relationships with publishers, vendors, and university stakeholders. Lead the assessment of electronic resource collections using usage statistics, cost-per-use analysis, financial data, and other assessment measures to support evidence-based collection development. Supervise, mentor, and support the Access & Discovery Librarian, providing leadership for the Electronic Resources Unit through workflow coordination, goal setting, and continuous improvement. Collaborate with the Access & Discovery Librarian to support authentication, discovery services, electronic resource access, and management of the Hunt and Hazy Libraries' A–Z database lists. Oversee electronic resource reporting, usage statistics, and data management using COUNTER/SUSHI standards, library analytics tools, and library management systems. Participate in library planning, committee work, professional development, and other initiatives that advance library services and the university's mission. About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Required Qualifications Master's degree in Library and Information Science (MLIS/MLS) from an ALA-accredited institution. Minimum of three years of progressively responsible professional experience managing electronic resources, budgets, and workflows in an academic library. Experience negotiating electronic resource licenses and vendor agreements. Experience with library management and discovery systems such as Ex Libris Alma and Primo VE (or comparable), authentication platforms such as OpenAthens, COUNTER/SUSHI standards, collection assessment and analytics tools (e.g., Alma Analytics and CELUS), and enterprise financial management systems. Demonstrated ability to supervise, mentor, and collaborate effectively with colleagues, vendors, and other campus stakeholders . Excellent written and verbal communication skills with strong attention to detail. Ability to collaborate effectively in a multi-campus environment. Preferred Qualifications Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Office and Microsoft 365 applications, particularly Excel. Experience working in a multi-campus academic library environment. Experience with collection assessment, cost-per-use analysis, or evidence-based collection development. Project management experience. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311841. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Prescott-AZ/Head-Coach--Wrestling_R311864": {
      "title": "Head Coach, Wrestling",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity       Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University (ERAU) seeks a dynamic, student-centered, and forward-thinking Head Coach, Wrestling to provide visionary leadership. Provide leadership and oversight of the intercollegiate men's wrestling program. This includes providing instruction of wrestling techniques, managing the program budget, supervision of assistant coaches, scheduling contests, coordinating travel and recruiting student-athletes.  For Primary Job Functions, Duties, or Accountabilities:  Provide fundamental and advanced instruction of wrestling techniques and philosophy to student-athletes. Administer all facets of the men's wrestling program, including: on-site management of all practices and games, supervise all assistant coaches, schedule matches, arrange for transportation, housing, meals for trips, purchase and care of uniforms and equipment, secure game management personnel (officials) for home events. Develop, implement and manage team budget in accordance of university APPM's. ensure that all team members adhere to University and NAIA guidelines with regard to academic and athletic eligibility; work with the Team Physician, Sports Medicine staff, and University Health Services to promote the health and safety of team members; monitor the academic progress of all team members; represent the Athletic Department and the Wrestling program at, NAIA regional, national, and other related meetings and events; perform assigned administrative duties with regard to University and NAIA requirements. Actively recruit and retain qualified incoming student-athletes who have interest men's wrestling.  Promote the men's wrestling program and pursue opportunities to fund-raise resources outside of the university budget. Develop relationships within the university to promote the wrestling program and student-athlete concept. Develop relationships within the community to promote the wrestling program and create community service opportunities; develop and execute fund-raising activities/camps/clinics to promote the wrestling program.      About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Qualifications    Bachelor's degree Wrestling techniques and coaching philosophy Knowledge and understanding of NAIA rules and regulations Strong computer skills including working with Microsoft Office 3-5 years of work related experience Preferred Qualifications     Master's degree Head coaching experience Collegiate coaching experience preferred To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311864. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Full CV   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
