    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Network-Engineer_R311749": {
      "title": "Network Engineer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity       Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University is seeking a Network Engineer to join the Information Technology team. Reporting to the Director of Network Engineering, this position is responsible for designing, implementing, administering, and supporting the University’s enterprise network and voice infrastructure. This role supports a hybrid environment, combining remote administrative responsibilities with on-campus work primarily based in Daytona Beach, Florida, assisting with network implementation, maintenance, and operational support across campus data centers and communication systems. The ideal candidate will have experience working in enterprise network environments using Cisco and/or Aruba technologies, with strong knowledge of routing, switching, wireless networking, firewalls, load balancing, and secure network architecture. Experience in hybrid or cloud-connected enterprise environments is highly desirable. Successful candidates are analytical, adaptable, and committed to continuous improvement. They communicate effectively, collaborate across technical teams, and provide high-quality customer service while supporting strategic IT initiatives. Preferred certifications include CCNP, Aruba Certified Switching Professional (ACSP), or equivalent advanced networking credentials. Embry-Riddle offers a collaborative work environment, professional development opportunities, a flexible summer schedule, and a comprehensive benefits package including health insurance, retirement plans, and generous education benefits. Key Responsibilities Network Operations & Support Monitor, troubleshoot, and resolve critical network performance and functionality issues Provide timely updates to management on outages and incidents Enforce operational policies and procedures to ensure high availability and reliability Respond to work orders and maintain accurate documentation in help desk systems Provide hands-on support for daily voice and data network operations Ensure IT equipment complies with industry standards and best practices Provide alternative solutions when necessary Network Design & Infrastructure Projects Participate in planning and implementation of infrastructure projects Design and develop network strategies and management practices Evaluate network changes and assess impact across campus systems Install, maintain, and support large-scale LAN/WAN and telecom services Coordinate low-voltage connectivity for campus construction projects Collaboration & Technical Consultation Collaborate with IT teams for troubleshooting, system configuration, and support Provide consulting, problem resolution, and needs analysis for stakeholders Support application and infrastructure integration efforts Planning & Governance Attend IT meetings, briefings, committees, and task forces Contribute to strategic and operational planning across IT departments Other Duties as Assigned Perform additional responsibilities in support of departmental and institutional needs. This is a hybrid position based in Daytona Beach that requires occasional on-campus work. Ideally, candidates should reside within approximately one hour of campus to accommodate in-office responsibilities as needed. About us    For nearly 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.     Today, our faculty, researchers and professiona l staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.     Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.     Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.      Qualifications Required Education Bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities 5+ years of experience in the design, operations, troubleshooting, and administration of enterprise Cisco or Aruba network environments (LAN, WAN, Wireless, Firewalls) Demonstrated proficiency in the configuration and management of Cisco or Aruba network infrastructure Strong working knowledge of network test and diagnostic equipment Expert-level understanding of Layer 2 technologies (e.g., Spanning Tree Protocol, 802.1Q, LACP) Expert-level knowledge of routing protocols (BGP, EIGRP, OSPF) Experience with network monitoring and telemetry tools (SNMP, NetFlow, sFlow, etc.) Extensive knowledge of Internet and IP-based services (DHCP, DNS, etc.) Experience supporting voice network systems and protocols (VoIP, RTP, SIP) Working knowledge of Avaya IP telephony administration Understanding of structured cabling standards, including copper and fiber optic environments Experience with cloud networking concepts and administration (Azure, AWS, GCP) Ability to plan, implement, and support technical initiatives in a complex enterprise or higher education environment Strong understanding of current IT networking and telecommunications trends and best practices Excellent customer service skills with a professional and solution-oriented approach Strong organizational and documentation skills Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with ability to work across technical and non-technical audiences Ability to maintain a professional demeanor in a collaborative environment Ability to document processes, procedures, and technical workflows accurately Commitment to IT core values, including accountability, continuous improvement, teamwork, and adaptability To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311749. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.     Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .      Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Research-Scientist--College-of-Aviation--Daytona-Beach-Campus_R311837": {
      "title": "Research Scientist, College of Aviation, Daytona Beach Campus",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University (ERAU), the world's largest fully accredited university specializing in aviation and aerospace, invites applications for a Research Scientist within the College of Aviation at the Daytona Beach Campus. This position supports a federally funded research program sponsored by the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) examining how the quality and type of flight training and operational experience influence pilot performance, proficiency, and aviation safety outcomes. Working as part of a multidisciplinary research team, the Research Scientist will contribute to advancing the science of aviation human factors and developing evidence-based recommendations to improve pilot training, qualification standards, and workforce readiness. The successful candidate will collaborate with researchers from Embry-Riddle, the University of Central Florida, Florida Institute of Technology, and industry partners, including major airlines, to produce impactful research that supports the future of aviation safety. Key Responsibilities The Research Scientist will: Conduct comprehensive literature reviews and synthesize existing research relevant to aviation human factors and pilot training. Design, develop, and execute research studies using flight simulators, field studies, surveys, and other experimental methodologies. Analyze quantitative and qualitative research data using appropriate statistical and analytical techniques. Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams of faculty, researchers, industry partners, and government stakeholders. Prepare technical reports, scholarly manuscripts, and other research deliverables for publication in peer-reviewed journals. Present research findings at national and international conferences, including organizations such as HFES, ISAP, and ICAP. Assist in the preparation of competitive grant proposals and support future sponsored research initiatives. Mentor undergraduate and graduate student researchers participating in project activities. ​Working Environment This position is based on ERAU's Daytona Beach Campus in a professional office and research environment. Periodic travel (approximately 0–2 trips per month), including occasional international travel, may be required depending on project needs. About us For nearly 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries. Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow. Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace. Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle! Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26. Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period. Generous Time Off: Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day. Qualifications Required Qualifications Ph.D. (or other terminal doctorate) in: Human Factors Cognitive Psychology Cognitive Science Industrial/Organizational Psychology or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated knowledge of research methodology and experimental design. Strong analytical, written, and verbal communication skills. Ability to work collaboratively within interdisciplinary research teams. Ability to manage multiple research activities and meet project deadlines. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates with experience in one or more of the following areas: Aviation human factors Pilot training and training effectiveness Flight simulation research Aviation safety research Flight training operations Scientific publication and technical writing Grant proposal development Application process/requirements Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R311837 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: Cover letter Full CV Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process) Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday. Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website .  Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Digital-Media-Specialist_R311766": {
      "title": "Digital Media Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity       Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University (ERAU) seeks a dynamic, student-centered, and forward-thinking Digital Media Specialist to provide visionary leadership. The Digital Media Specialist is a key member of the Digital Strategy team responsible for creating high-quality, social-first multimedia content to support the university’s brand and enrollment marketing efforts. This role focuses heavily on video production and editing, developing engaging content tailored for platforms such as YouTube, TikTok, Meta and other digital channels. Working closely with the Associate Director of Social Media Strategy, the Specialist captures, edits and delivers compelling video content, including student stories, event coverage and day-to-day brand moments. Content is primarily captured using mobile and lightweight equipment (e.g., iPhone, DJI or similar tools) while also leveraging professional DSLR, mirrorless and cinema-style camera systems as needed to support higher-level productions and special projects. The Specialist should have working knowledge of professional camera, audio and lighting equipment and be comfortable operating in a variety of production environments, though the role is primarily focused on agile, in-the-field content creation rather than studio-based production work. The Digital Media Specialist demonstrates strong technical proficiency in video editing tools, such as Adobe Premiere Pro or similar software, with the ability to produce polished, professional edits optimized for platform-specific formats. They have a strong understanding of social video formats, including both short-form and long-form content, and how they perform across platforms, particularly YouTube and TikTok. The Specialist applies this knowledge to create content that aligns with platform best practices and audience behavior and is able to provide recommendations on how to effectively leverage these platforms, including content structure, pacing and storytelling approaches to maximize engagement and reach. The Specialist contributes to both organic and paid initiatives by developing multimedia assets that align with campaign goals and creative direction. They are responsible for executing video concepts, repurposing content across platforms and ensuring all deliverables meet brand standards and best practices. This role emphasizes hands-on content creation and post-production, requiring a strong eye for storytelling, pacing and visual quality. The Specialist applies performance insights and platform knowledge to refine content and enhance overall effectiveness, while staying current on trends, tools and emerging formats. The Specialist works both independently and collaboratively, managing multiple projects and delivering high-quality content that supports university priorities and elevates the institution’s digital presence.   About us     For nearly 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.     Today, our faculty, researchers and professiona l staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.     Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.     Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Qualifications   Bachelor's degree in Digital Media, Communications, Film, Marketing or a related field 3-5 years of related work experience in creative design, marketing, video editing or other applicable role Strong proficiency in video editing software (e.g., Adobe Premiere Pro, Final Cut Pro or similar), with the ability to produce polished, professional edits optimized for social platforms Demonstrated ability to capture and create high-quality, social-first video content using mobile and lightweight equipment (e.g., iPhone, DJI or similar tools) Strong understanding of social media video formats, including short-form and long-form content, particularly for YouTube and TikTok Knowledge of platform best practices, including pacing, hooks, storytelling structure and audience engagement strategies Ability to translate creative concepts into engaging video content that aligns with brand standards and campaign goals Strong storytelling skills with an understanding of visual composition, timing and narrative flow Experience optimizing video content for performance, including titles, thumbnails, captions and formatting Ability to analyze content performance using platform analytics and apply insights to improve future content Working knowledge of accessibility standards for video content, including captions, on-screen text and visual clarity Strong attention to detail and ability to maintain consistency and quality across all content Ability to manage multiple projects and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment Strong collaboration and communication skills, with the ability to work effectively with cross-functional teams and stakeholders Ability to work independently, take direction and execute projects with minimal supervision To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311766. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Full CV   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.     Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .          Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Prescott-AZ/Graphic-Designer_R311784": {
      "title": "Graphic Designer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity       Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University (ERAU) seeks a dynamic, student-centered, and forward-thinking Graphic Designer to provide visionary leadership. **This is an in-person position.** The Graphic Designer is responsible for the layout, design, and production of marketing and communications materials that support a consistent and cohesive university brand. This is a full-time, on-site administrative and professional staff position based at our Prescott, Arizona campus, reporting to the Director of Creative and Brand Strategy. This role requires a self-sufficient designer with a strong portfolio, excellent typography skills, and exceptional attention to detail. The Graphic Designer must be able to manage multiple concurrent projects while also executing focused, detail-driven creative work. The position contributes to the development of innovative design solutions and collaborates with campus partners and colleagues across a creative team environment. A strong emphasis is placed on translating brand strategy into high-quality, production-ready deliverables, particularly in print and multi-page design work. This includes a strong understanding of layout, typography, color, and print production processes. The Graphic Designer supports a diverse set of higher education audiences, including prospective students, donors, alums, faculty, staff, and parents. The role requires flexibility, creative problem-solving, and a commitment to continuous professional growth and collaboration across the university community. Primary Job Functions and Duties: Develop creative concepts and visual solutions that align with project goals and university brand standards. Execute designs for a variety of formats (publications, campaigns, digital assets, environmental graphics, etc.). Prepare production-ready files for print and digital distribution. Ensure accuracy, quality, accessibility, and consistency across all deliverables. Collaborate with clients, copywriters, and the graphic design team to execute designs and adhere to the university brand, based on direction provided by the Creative Director and the Director of Creative and Brand Strategy. Stay current with design trends, tools, and best practices in higher education marketing and visual communication. Contribute ideas to improve creative workflows, processes, and team collaboration. Secondary Job Functions and Duties: Participate in weekly creative team meetings and one-on-one meetings to discuss project workload, priorities, and performance. Demonstrate a strong ability to collaborate with team members and stakeholders, incorporating feedback to strengthen creative solutions. Maintain accurate project status updates and task management within the department’s project management system. Perform other duties as assigned by the Creative Director or Director of Creative and Brand Strategy. About us     For nearly 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.     Today, our faculty, researchers and professiona l staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.     Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.     Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Required Education: Bachelor's Degree Area of Concentration: Graphic Design Required Skills, Knowledge and Abilities: Ability to work in a complex university environment that is fast-paced, deadline-driven and collaborative. Strong ability to communicate and present designs effectively, including client pitches, as well as to welcome feedback and incorporate requested changes as projects evolve. Required Years of Work-Related Experience: 3-5 years Type of Work-Related Experience: Creative/Marketing Agency or higher-ed experience is preferred. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R311784. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Full CV   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.     Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .        Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
