    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Sports-Medicine-Fellow_R311551": {
      "title": "Sports Medicine Fellow",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Embry-Riddle: Celebrating 100 Years of Leadership in Aviation and Aerospace   As Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University marks its Centennial, we proudly celebrate 100 years of advancing the future of flight and aerospace education. With vibrant residential campuses in Daytona Beach, FL, and Prescott, AZ — and a Worldwide network spanning   nearly 120   global locations — Embry-Riddle stands as the world’s largest aviation and aerospace university.   For a century, we have led innovation in STEM education, serving more than 30,000 students around the globe. Our   cutting-edge   programs in Applied Science, Aviation, Business, Technology, Engineering, Safety, Security, and Space empower the next generation of leaders to shape the future of flight, exploration, and discovery.   As we launch our next century, we   remain   committed to excellence, innovation, and preparing graduates who will transform industries and redefine what is possible. The Opportunity: Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University (ERAU) in Daytona Beach, FL. Is offering one (1) Sports Medicine Fellowship for the 2026-2027 academic year. The successful candidate will be responsible for sport coverage as assigned by the Associate Athletic Director/Health and Sport Performance and will have the opportunity to practice and expand their clinical athletic training skills by obtaining hands-on experience under the guidance of the seven full-time staff athletic trainers. The fellow will assist with the daily operation of the two on-campus athletic health care centers, assist with Team Physician(s) clinical athletic training room rounds, work and communicate with coaches, strength and conditioning staff, and other members of the multi-disciplinary athletic health care team. Embry-Riddle Intercollegiate Athletics sponsors 20 NCAA Division II sports, and is a proud member of the Sunshine State Conference (SSC). The internship is a 10-month position. Total compensation will be approximately $12,500 per semester plus a university meal plan. Start date will be August 1, 2026 for a term not to exceed May 31, 2027. Depending on sport assignment, there will be considerable time off during the month of December. Housing and health insurance are NOT included. Please visit http://www . erauathletics.com to review the athletic program, the athletic training staff, and for additional information about ERAU Sports Medicine. Qualifications"
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Postdoctoral-Scholar--Daytona-Beach-Campus_R311531": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar, Daytona Beach Campus",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-19\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University (ERAU), Daytona Beach Campus, invites applications for a full-time Postdoctoral Scholar position in the field of magnetospheric physics and space instrumentation. The successful candidate will contribute to cutting-edge research focused on the design and development of a miniature particle detector, as well as the analysis of satellite observations and numerical simulation results related to the Earth’s magnetosphere and space plasma environment. This position offers an exciting opportunity to work in a collaborative research environment at one of the world’s leading aerospace-focused universities. Position Responsibilities: Participate in the design, development, testing, and integration of a miniature particle detector for space applications. Analyze satellite measurements and numerical simulation results in the field of magnetospheric physics and space plasma science. Contribute to the development of data analysis tools and scientific interpretation of observational and modeling results. Prepare manuscripts for publication in peer-reviewed journals and present research findings at scientific conferences. Assist with proposal development and contribute to externally funded research activities. Collaborate with faculty, students, and external research partners on interdisciplinary research initiatives. Mentoring and Career Development: This position includes a structured mentoring plan designed to support the professional growth of an early-career postdoctoral scientist and foster the development of independent research capabilities. Mentoring activities will include: Weekly one-on-one meetings focused on research progress, manuscript preparation, proposal development, and career planning. Regular group meetings to encourage collaboration, scientific communication, and presentation skills. Guidance in building a competitive research portfolio, securing external funding, leading research projects, and publishing high-impact research. Career development support will include: Periodic discussions to define long-term career goals and identify funding opportunities. Collaborative establishment of short- and medium-term milestones, including manuscript submissions and grant applications. Opportunities to take increasing ownership of research activities, including project leadership, collaboration management, and mentoring junior trainees. The overall goal of this mentoring framework is to support the successful transition of the postdoctoral scholar toward research independence and long-term career advancement. Embry-Riddle: Celebrating 100 Years of Leadership in Aviation and Aerospace  As Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University marks its Centennial, we proudly celebrate 100 years of advancing the future of flight and aerospace education. With vibrant residential campuses in Daytona Beach, FL, and Prescott, AZ — and a Worldwide network spanning nearly 120 global locations — Embry-Riddle stands as the world’s largest aviation and aerospace university. For a century, we have led innovation in STEM education, serving more than 30,000 students around the globe. Our cutting-edge programs in Applied Science, Aviation, Business, Technology, Engineering, Safety, Security, and Space empower the next generation of leaders to shape the future of flight, exploration, and discovery. As we launch our next century, we remain committed to excellence, innovation, and preparing graduates who will transform industries and redefine what is possible.  Click here to take a virtual tour of the Daytona Beach Campus! Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle!    Generous Time Off: Enjoy 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year’s Day. Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26. Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period. Personal Leave: Relax with 12 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.  Qualifications Required Education and Qualifications: Ph.D. in Physics, Space Physics, Aerospace Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a closely related field by the start date of employment. Demonstrated background in space physics, magnetospheric physics, plasma physics, or related disciplines. Experience with scientific data analysis and/or numerical simulations. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work effectively both independently and collaboratively in a research environment. Preferred Qualifications Experience with space instrumentation or particle detector development. Familiarity with satellite data analysis techniques. Experience with numerical modeling and scientific programming (e.g., Python, MATLAB, IDL, C/C++). Record of peer-reviewed publications and conference presentations. Application process/requirements Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R311531 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: Cover letter Full CV 2-page Research statement Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process) Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday. Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website . Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Prescott-AZ/Assistant-Chief-Flight-Instructor_R309898": {
      "title": "Assistant Chief Flight Instructor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-18\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Discover Your Future with Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University!        Embry-Riddle: A Global Leader in Aviation and Aerospace        With vibrant campuses in Daytona Beach, FL and Prescott, AZ, plus a Worldwide network across approximately 120 locations, Embry-Riddle stands as the world’s largest aviation and aerospace university. For over 95 years, we've been pioneering education in STEM fields, serving over 11,600 residential students and 19,200 globally in the 2023-24 academic year with cutting-edge programs in Applied Science, Aviation, Business, Technology, Engineering, Safety, Security, and Space.   To complete a virtual tour of the Prescott campus and check out Prescott Campus Future Flythrough, please visit the links below: https://prescott.erau.edu/admissions/tour-details https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rQeMUHG4AU4 Opportunity:    Join the Aviation and Aerospace vanguard!    Step into a dynamic role with Embry Riddle Aeronautical University, where innovation meets opportunity. Be part of a leading institution that’s at the forefront of aviation, aerospace, and STEM education. We offer an exciting environment, cutting-edge projects, and the chance to influence tomorrow. Ready to make a difference? Take flight with Embry-Riddle and explore this diverse career opportunity today.     The Flight Department at the Prescott campus of Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University is seeking Assistant Chief Flight Instructors to support the Flight Department. Job duties include: Provide overall management for approximately 20 instructors and 150 to 200 flight students.  Responsible for overall training quality and providing excellent student service. Ensure proper conduct and enforcement of effective training and safety standards, regulations, and procedures as established. Maintain and ensure compliance with current University and FAA policies and procedures. Assist, counsel, and resolve problems and, as needed, make recommendations for disciplinary action of all students and instructors designated to your supervision. Attend weekly Flight Training Manager meeting with Chief Flight Instructor. Attend weekly Staff meeting with Department Chair. Prepare for and attend daily Student Progress Briefings with Chief Flight Instructor and Department Chair. Prepare for and conduct monthly Team meetings with assigned Instructor Pilots. Review and adjust as needed the daily instructor schedule. Ensure maximum utilization of instructor, aircraft, and flight training device resources. Ensure assigned students are scheduled to meet their required activities. Verify student eligibility at the beginning of each assigned ground school section. Meet with Students/Family regarding training progress. Participate in New Hire instructor hiring process as requested by Chief Flight Instructor. Conduct stage checks and end of course tests as assigned. Other tasks as assigned by the Chief Flight Instructor. Embry-Riddle's Prescott Campus is respected worldwide for cutting-edge instruction and training for tomorrow’s aviation, aerospace, security, and intelligence leaders. Prescott is a mile-high city and its climate reflects seasonable weather excellent for flying. Daytime averages are 80°F in the summer and 45°F in the winter. At 5,000 ft. above sea level, it boasts a mild climate, clean air, pristine wilderness areas, and nearby national forests. The university is a small, private, residential university in the mountains of Arizona with approximately 3,500 students. Staff/faculty/student interaction is highly valued and is a central theme of our campus. It is located 100 miles north of Phoenix and 120 miles south of the Grand Canyon.     Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle!    Generous Time Off:  Relax with 15 days of personal leave in your first year. Enjoy 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year’s Day.  Health Benefits:  Experience comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, along with wellness programs that include preventive care and fitness memberships. Our flexible spending and health savings accounts simplify managing healthcare costs. Join a workplace that prioritizes your health—because your journey to wellness should be rewarding! Buckle up for a healthier, happier you!  Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes an annual 6% gift of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution, with no vesting period.  Application process/requirements To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R309898 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: Cover letter Full Resume Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process) Current Embry-Riddle employees:  Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday. Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website . Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. Must hold a Commercial Pilot Certificate and a Flight Instructor Certificate with Airplane Single-Engine Land and Instrument Airplane privileges. Must hold at least a 2nd class medical certificate. Meet the minimum requirements for Assistant Chief under 14 CFR part 141. (Preferred) Required skills,  knowledge, abilities: Analytical skills with an in depth knowledge of information systems and technical expertise with Microsoft operating systems, Access, Excel, PowerPoint, Word, Outlook/email, and Internet end-user applications"
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Lab-Manager--Department-of-Physical-Sciences--Daytona-Beach-Campus_R311334": {
      "title": "Lab Manager, Department of Physical Sciences, Daytona Beach Campus",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity   The Department of Physical Sciences at the Daytona Beach Campus seeks applicants for the position of Lab Manager. This position provides essential support to the department in the maintenance , use, and development of its teaching and research laboratory equipment. This individual is responsible for ensuring the smooth function of the department's teaching labs and assists both faculty and students in the development and implementation of new research capabilities. Responsibilities include: Maintaining, troubleshooting, and repairing laboratory equipment and electronics (oscilloscopes, power supplies, optics, detectors, vacuum systems, instrumentation, etc.). Supporting faculty and staff in developing, setting up, and adapting experiments for teaching and research. Overseeing laboratory safety procedures in collaboration with faculty and the university’s safety office. Coordinating with vendors for service and procurement of parts and supplies. Providing technical training and guidance for faculty, graduate teaching assistants, and students as needed. Embry-Riddle: Celebrating 100 Years of Leadership in Aviation and Aerospace   As Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University marks its Centennial, we proudly celebrate 100 years of advancing the future of flight and aerospace education. With vibrant residential campuses in Daytona Beach, FL, and Prescott, AZ — and a Worldwide network spanning nearly 120 global locations — Embry-Riddle stands as the world’s largest aviation and aerospace university. For a century, we have led innovation in STEM education, serving more than 30,000 students around the globe. Our cutting-edge programs in Applied Science, Aviation, Business, Technology, Engineering, Safety, Security, and Space empower the next generation of leaders to shape the future of flight, exploration, and discovery. As we launch our next century, we remain committed to excellence, innovation, and preparing graduates who will transform industries and redefine what is possible.   Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle!    Generous Time Off: Enjoy 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year’s Day. Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26. Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period. Personal Leave: Relax with 12 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year. Qualifications Required Education and Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in engineering physics, physics, engineering, electronics technology, or a related field, or equivalent professional experience. D emonstrated hands-on skills in electronics troubleshooting, instrumentation, and laboratory hardware maintenance. Strong organizational and communication skills. Application process/requirements To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number   R311334 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: Cover letter Full Resume Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process) ​​ Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday. Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website . Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Prescott-AZ/Assistant-Athletic-Trainer_R311345": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Embry-Riddle: Celebrating 100 Years of Leadership in Aviation and Aerospace     As Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University marks its Centennial, we proudly celebrate 100 years of advancing the future of flight and aerospace education. With vibrant residential campuses in Daytona Beach, FL, and Prescott, AZ — and a Worldwide network spanning nearly 120 global locations — Embry-Riddle stands as the world’s largest aviation and aerospace university.     For a century, we have led innovation in STEM education, serving more than 30,000 students around the globe. Our cutting-edge programs in Applied Science, Aviation, Business, Technology, Engineering, Safety, Security, and Space empower the next generation of leaders to shape the future of flight, exploration, and discovery.     As we launch our next century, we remain committed to excellence, innovation, and preparing graduates who will transform industries and redefine what is possible.   The Opportunity   Job Responsibilities Include: Work under the supervision of the Director of Athletic Training and be responsible for the following:  prevention of athletic injuries and illnesses, evaluation of athletic injuries, treatment of athletic injuries, providing education and counseling to student-athletes about their injury/illness. Oversee the CPR/AED and First Aid education for all Athletic Staff. Oversee the day-to-day operations of the athletic training room. Travels with both male and female teams. Participates in inventory management of supplies Documents and maintains student-athlete PHI (i.e. physicals, injury reports, rehabilitation, etc.) into the SportsWare Online system. Maintains appropriate communication with the Director of Athletic Training, student-athletes, coaches, and physicians. Maintains appropriate communication and attends meetings within the Department of Athletics. Obtains, creates and maintains an athletic calendar of events. Will coordinate and maintain records for all athletic physical examinations for all student-athletes. Completes required CEU’s for NATA and Arizona Licensure Remain in good standing with the NATA and Arizona Athletic Trainer’s Licensure. Develops, communicates and enforces Embry Riddle Athletic Training Policy & Procedures for athletes. Works more than the traditional 40 hours per week, which may include many weekends (including Sundays), nights and holidays. Must possess a valid driver’s license for transportation of team in vans and the ability to travel for team practices and competition. Other duties as assigned. Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle!   Health Benefits:   Experience comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, along with wellness programs that include preventive care and fitness memberships. Our flexible spending and health savings accounts simplify managing healthcare costs. Join a workplace that prioritizes your health—because your journey to wellness should be rewarding! Buckle up for a healthier, happier you!   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.     Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes an annual 6% gift of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution, with no vesting period.   Generous Time Off:   Generous Time Off: Relax with 18 days of personal leave in your first year. Enjoy 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year’s Day.      Qualifications Required Education and Qualifications:   Bachelor degree in exercise physiology/health education, sports medicine or a related field preferred. BOC Certification for Athletic Training Arizona Athletic Training License Current CPR/AED certification.     Application process/requirements   To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number   R311345 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Full Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
