    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Prescott-AZ/Assistant-Professor-of-Professional-Writing_R309304": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Professional Writing",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-06-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Discover Your Future with Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University!        Embry-Riddle: A Global Leader in Aviation and Aerospace        With vibrant campuses in Daytona Beach, FL and Prescott, AZ, plus a Worldwide network across approximately 120 locations, Embry-Riddle stands as the world’s largest aviation and aerospace university. For over 95 years, we've been pioneering education in STEM fields, serving over 11,600 residential students and 19,200 globally in the 2023-24 academic year with cutting-edge programs in Applied Science, Aviation, Business, Technology, Engineering, Safety, Security, and Space.     To complete a virtual tour of the Prescott campus and check out Prescott Campus Future Flythrough, please visit the links below:   https://prescott.erau.edu/admissions/tour-details   https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rQeMUHG4AU4       Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle!    Generous Time Off:  Enjoy 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year’s Day.  Health Benefits:  Experience comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, along with wellness programs that include preventive care and fitness memberships. Our flexible spending and health savings accounts simplify managing healthcare costs. Join a workplace that prioritizes your health—because your journey to wellness should be rewarding! Buckle up for a healthier, happier you!  Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes an annual 6% gift of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution, with no vesting period.  Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University recognizes the value of diversity and is dedicated to fostering a positive climate in which all students, faculty, and staff are encouraged in their professional, social, and intellectual pursuits. Embry-Riddle is committed to providing equal employment opportunity  and affirmative action for qualified individuals. The University does not tolerate discrimination on the basis of race, creed, color, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, gender identity, genetic information, disability, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law.       Opportunity:        Join the Aviation and Aerospace vanguard!    Step into a dynamic role with Embry Riddle Aeronautical University, where innovation meets opportunity. Be part of a leading institution that’s at the forefront of aviation, aerospace, and STEM education. We offer an exciting environment, cutting-edge projects, and the chance to influence tomorrow. Ready to make a difference? Take flight with Embry-Riddle and explore this diverse career opportunity today.   The Department of Humanities and Communication at the College of Arts and Sciences in Prescott, Arizona is seeking to fill two 9-month, full-time, non-tenure track faculty positions starting in August 2025 or January 2026. These are ranked, renewable positions, with opportunities for promotion. Responsibilities: Teaching load is 24 credit hours per academic year (fall and spring semesters). Summer teaching is available and additionally compensated. Primary teaching responsibilities include first year composition, professional writing, and rhetoric, with the opportunity to teach cultural studies, and humanities. The successful candidate will collaborate with other faculty on developing new courses and perform course and program assessments. Preference will be given to applicants with experience in collaborative teaching, writing across the curriculum, and practical teaching students in STEM majors. Successful candidates will also support the department, college, and campus through service.  Qualifications Minimum Ph.D. in Writing Studies, Rhetoric and Composition, Technical and Professional Writing, or related field at the time of the appointment. Preferred We are interested in candidates with expertise in one or more of the following areas: Experience in participating in programmatic assessment and curriculum design for first-year writing and humanities courses. Experience teaching technical writing and/or business communication courses that provide practical rhetorical knowledge to students in various majors.  Collaborative teaching, team-teaching, or writing across the curriculum Professional experience writing in the disciplines, e.g., in intelligence-gathering communities, the gaming industry, engineering / simulations industries. To ensure full consideration, please apply online by uploading 1) a letter of application, 2) a CV, and 3) the names and contact information of three professional references.  Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Only electronic applications will be considered.  Questions may be addressed to the Department Chair Dr. Matt Haslam, haslamm@erau.edu."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Student-Success_R309369": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Student Success",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-03-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Assistant Manager for Student Success plays a vital role in ensuring ERAU students receive the support they need to succeed academically and personally. The incumbent will enhance student experience, retention and success for ERAU students by providing integrated advising, career planning, and pastoral  support. This role bridges advising, career services, and industry partners to support students in achieving their educational and professional goals, as well as extends the connection between graduates and students at ERAU. Key Responsibilities: Student Success Monitor and conduct proactive advising for at-risk students and deploy targeted interventions Enhance student learning and support through mentorship scheme Spearhead and implement wellness initiatives and programs to support student wellbeing Coordinate and/or provide interventions and support for students with learning gaps Facilitate student success through ERAU’s Global Learning, Relevance to industries/community, Open communication, Worth and wellbeing (GROW) model Identify, coach and motivate students to represent ERAU in industry competition, MICE-related events to facilitate student exposure Deliver, where possible, or support the course instruction for College Success (UNIV 101) Provide guidance to students about Study Abroad and Eagle Mobility programs offered within the university Partner faculty members and the Office of Student Services for effective progress monitoring practices Alumni and Career Services Partner internal stakeholders and industry partners to facilitate internship and job placements Plan and execute lunch time talks, industry visits, career fairs and/or other learning journey to enhance student learning Coordinate career coaching sessions with faculty members and/or mentors Organise and coordinate alumni events and engagement with ERAU graduates Data and Compliance Implement system for progress monitoring to track student progress and growth Work closely with Office of Data Management to use student performance data to identify at-risk students and develop targeted interventions Use student performance data to drive decision-making and continuous improvement in student outcomes and address barriers to student retention Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in education, psychology, or related field. Master’s degree preferred. Prior experience in student success or advising, or a similar role working with diverse student population, strongly preferred. Other equivalent experience may be considered. Ability to build rapport, actively listen, and establish positive relationships with students from various backgrounds. Proven track record in analytical and problem-solving skills, including the ability to collect, and interpret data. Strong communication and collaboration skills."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Singapore/Executive--Student-Recruitment_R308921": {
      "title": "Executive, Student Recruitment",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-12-18\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Discover Your Future with Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University! Embry-Riddle: A Global Leader in Aviation and Aerospace With vibrant campuses in Daytona Beach, FL and Prescott, AZ, plus a Worldwide network across approximately 120 locations, Embry-Riddle stands as the world’s largest aviation and aerospace university. For over 95 years, we've been pioneering education in STEM fields, serving over 11,600 residential students and 19,200 globally in the 2023-24 academic year with cutting-edge programs in Applied Science, Aviation, Business, Technology, Engineering, Safety, Security, and Space. The Opportunity: Our Singapore office, ERAU Asia, is looking for an individual with a dynamic personality who loves to speak in public and engage with large audiences to fill the role of the Executive, Student Recruitment. The Student Recruitment Executive leverages these innate skills to represent and promote ERAU Asia in a variety of forums, build relationships with prospective students, families, counsellors and consultants, fulfils the recruitment plan to meet enrollment goals. The Executive maintains continuous contact with prospective students during the application and admissions process and stays current on industry and campus news.  The Student Recruitment Executive at ERAU Asia is the largest knowledge base for all things related to ERAU Asia. Responsibilities include: Actively engage with prospective students in various communication channels; build relationships with students, parents and counsellors, answer their queries related to academic programs, admission criteria, financial aid, campus life and more. Support the Assistant Director for Student Recruitment in the development of student recruitment marketing & outreach strategy, measure progress and provide reports to the team. Leverage on CRM system to maintain prospects and proactively reach out to prospective students to follow up on interest, monitor progress and achieve established KPIs and demonstrate positive ROI on recruitment events. Conduct campus tours for prospective students and families, showcasing the university’s facilities and student life; coordinate and participate in all local and international student recruitment related events, including but not limited to logistics arrangement, coordination with organizing parties and setting up the booth. Conduct and/or support in pre-course counselling for prospective students and work with the Office of Admissions to follow up on outstanding applications; maintain accurate student interactions and records in the CRM system. Work closely with the Office of Admissions to monitor prospect progression and meet enrollment targets by converting leads into matriculations. Manage and maintain the accuracy and quantity of marketing and recruitment collateral. This includes, but is not limited to banners, pamphlets and posters. Qualifications At least a Bachelor’s degree in any field. 1 to 3 years of work-related experience. Must be willing to travel approximately 50% of the time. Must be able to accommodate some night and/or weekend work. Proficient in using CRM systems and database. Prior experience engaging with overseas education partners is preferred. Possess excellent verbal and written communication skills. Strong proficiency in English is essential to the role. Customer-centric, enjoy meeting and speaking with people. Ability to work independently or as a team player."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Singapore/Unmanned-Aircraft-System--UAS--Instructor_R305184": {
      "title": "Adjunct Uncrewed Aircraft System (UAS) Instructor",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-04-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Description The Office of Professional Education & Training is looking for avid and qualified UAS license holders to assist the Chief Instructor in conducting practical training for CAAS Uncrewed Aerial Pilot License (UAPL) courses.  The UAPL courses will be fully compliant to CAAS requirements and Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University requirements.   Qualifications Knowledge with UAS operations, familiar with CAAS ANR 101 regulations and have a good understanding of UAS airspace.   Strong communication, presentation and critical thinking skills required. Teaching experience especially in practical for UAS preferred. Experience flying a variety of small UAS drones such as DJI Phantom, Mavic and Inspire. Additional experience in flight planning and post processing software preferred. Possession of the following qualifications is ideal: - FAA CFR Part 107 Remote Pilot Certificate - UA Pilot License issued by CAAS (25kg) - AUVSI Trusted Operator Program (TOP) Level 1 - AUVSI Trusted Operator Program (TOP) Level 2 - AUVSI Trusted Operator Program (TOP) Level 3  Each course will last for 5 days. Instructor is expected to support the 28-hour practical training over the 5 days, as well as the preparation work for the training (estimated around 2 days). Instructor will be remunerated SGD1,260 for each course upon satisfactory performance."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Singapore/Adjunct-Faculty--Finance---Accounting_R302174": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Finance & Accounting",
      "description": "Start date: 2021-10-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Description Backed by the world’s largest and oldest university specializing in aviation and aerospace, Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University, the Asia campus is looking for a passionate educator to support the course instruction to groom aviation leaders of tomorrow. The identified educator should demonstrate passion and extensive knowledge in the subject matter and be open to using engaging visuals, technologies and methods to facilitate knowledge transfer and interaction with undergraduate and graduate students. The adjunct faculty can look forward to teaching the following modules: Corporate Finance Budgeting and Finance for R&D Investments International Finance Global Economic Analysis Financial Accounting Managerial Accounting Business Accounting The above modules are non-exhaustive. Qualifications At least a master’s or doctoral degree in Finance and/or Accounting Confident and comfortable to engage with large groups Professional experience in the aviation industry or teaching experience at a higher educational institution will be advantageous Note: This is an adjunct position where the faculty will be engaged for a nine-week term.  The faculty member will be required to teach up to six (6) hours per week in class.  Each term consists of eight weeks of teaching and one week of examination and grading.  The adjunct faculty must be available to teach during the day during weekdays and/or weekends. We apologise that only shortlisted candidates will be contacted for interviews."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Associate-Registrar-for-Technology-and-Compliance_R312113": {
      "title": "Associate Registrar for Technology and Compliance",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity: Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University is now hiring Associate Registrar for Technology and Compliance. The Associate Registrar for Technology and Compliance provides technical leadership and management expertise to support the development, enhancement, maintenance, and implementation of technology solutions central to the University’s mission. With direction from the University Registrar, this Associate Registrar position partners with the division leadership team to foster an environment that sets clear expectations and is cohesive, imaginative, data-driven and results-oriented, furthering a culture that is guided by rigorous analysis, testing and data-informed planning. This Associate Registrar position exhibits a high level of creative problem-solving ability, resourcefulness, and the competence needed to conduct business process evaluations, develop short- and long-term technology goals, make recommendations, and execute projects to improve processes and technologies while ensuring compliance with university policies, accreditation standards and state/federal regulations. This position collaborates closely with internal and external stakeholders such as Information Technology Services, Imaging, administrative staff, faculty, and third-party vendors and is critical in developing a comprehensive strategic and tactical technology infrastructure for the Office of the Registrar in support of the University’s Strategic Plan. With responsibility for managing seven employees (five business analysts and two transcript/record specialists) and supporting University-wide constituents and initiatives, this is a position for a highly motivated, skilled manager of people, programs and technology. Responsibilities include the following: Staff Development Provide employees with timely and challenging professional development opportunities for improving their skills and increasing their office and institutional effectiveness to deliver the highest quality of technology-driven services for our constituents. Maintain productivity and quality metrics for the team and office. Ensure office staff are trained on system functionality, business processes, data standards, security requirements, reporting tools, and applicable policies. Collaborate and enhance relationships within the office and across the University. Operations Serve as the technical expert for core student information system applications and related technologies These information system applications include, but are not limited to, National Student Clearinghouse, NSLDS, Campus Solutions, Civitas, CourseDog, Parchment, Canusia, Imaging, Sharepoint and other products related to registrar responsibilities that interface with the student module. Coordinate the accurate and timely transmission of required data and reports to internal and external entities. Analyze operational and business processes to identify opportunities for increased efficiency, improved data integrity, and enhanced service delivery. Respond to ad hoc reporting requests and provide analysis to support institutional decision-making. Troubleshoot system and process issues, coordinate problem resolution, and communicate impacts and recommended solutions to appropriate stakeholders. Maintain current documentation for critical systems, processes, procedures, and recurring operational activities. Communications and Change Management Develop clear communications regarding system changes, technical requirements, process impacts, implementation timelines, outages, enhancements, and operational expectations. Translate complex technical and functional information into practical guidance for students, faculty, staff, administrators, and campus partners. Review communications and instructional materials for technical accuracy, clarity, consistency, grammar, and alignment with University policies. Coordinate change-management communications to support successful adoption of new systems, processes, reports, and technology-enabled services. Compliance Ensure compliance with federal, state, and university regulations and policies; design reports to support data integrity and access/role security. Fulfill NSC, NSLDS, FVT/GE, internal audit, single audit and other federal reporting obligations within regulatory standards. Delegate user role provisioning to campus registrar staff to process. Know and apply FERPA and other data security policies. Oversee and approve all sensitive data requests. Other Job functions include: Represent the Office of the Registrar on enterprise technology, student information system, data governance, and process-improvement committees. Participate in University projects involving academic records, enrollment, curriculum, registration, graduation, reporting, and student services. Work additional hours during peak academic periods, system implementations, reporting deadlines, and special events as operational needs require. Perform other duties as assigned by the University Registrar. About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.         Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Required Qualifications: Master’s Degree required; Candidates with a bachelor’s degree and/or at least 10+ years of leadership experience in higher education may be considered. Minimum of 5-10 years of related work experience.  Demonstrated proficiency with enterprise systems like Ellucian Banner , Workday Student , or PeopleSoft. Experience with database query tools, degree audit systems (e.g., DegreeWorks), and regulatory reporting to federal or state bodies. Required skills, knowledge, abilities: Expertise to lead teams and an open and collaborative leadership style that builds trust across constituencies among all campuses. A passion for advancing diversity and equity and enhancing inclusiveness; experience bringing individuals of varying backgrounds and differing viewpoints together to find common ground. Extensive knowledge of computer systems, data mining and information technology, along with demonstrated experience developing and utilizing that technology, in a large and complex university setting. Demonstrated enthusiastic and creative use of information technology systems to provide solutions to the academic community, including the use of AI to improve processes and procedures. An interest in engagement of campus constituents. Excellent interpersonal and organization skills. Confidence and excitement about change. Sound judgment and integrity. Outstanding written and oral communication as well as critical thinking skills. Ability to multi-task; a self-starter with a positive attitude and strong work ethic. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R312113 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Digital-Collections-Specialist_R312128": {
      "title": "Digital Collections Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Hunt Library seeks a detail-oriented and technically skilled Digital Collections Specialist  to manage and contribute to digitization and digital collections initiatives within Archives & Special Collections. This position will preserve and expand access to the library’s unique collections by preparing materials for digitization, organizing and managing digital assets, creating and reviewing metadata, and supporting digital preservation and quality control practices. This position offers an opportunity to apply existing library or cultural heritage experience while developing and expanding specialized skills in digital collections, digitization, and digital preservation. Demonstrated technical aptitude, responsive communication, attention to detail, and willingness to learn are highly valued. The successful candidate will work collaboratively with library staff, exercise sound judgment when managing projects and digital assets, follow established standards and workflows, and communicate proactively about project progress, questions, and challenges. About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Required Education Bachelor's degree. Minimum Qualifications 1–3 years of experience working in a library, archives, museum, historical organization, or other cultural heritage environment. Demonstrated attention to detail and ability to maintain accuracy when working with large quantities of information, digital files, and descriptive data. Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple projects, prioritize work, and follow established procedures and workflows. Demonstrated computer proficiency and ability to learn and effectively use new software, systems, and technologies. Ability to work independently with moderate to minimal guidance and collaborate successfully with colleagues on projects and initiatives. Effective written and verbal communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Experience with digitization, scanning, digital photography, or image processing. Experience with digital asset management systems, digital collections platforms, repositories, archival management systems, or related library technologies such as JSTOR Stewardship, ArchivesSpace, CONTENTdm, or Alma Familiarity with metadata concepts or standards such as Dublin Core, MARC, XML, or similar schemas. Familiarity with digital preservation concepts and practices. Experience organizing and managing large quantities of digital files. Experience with relational databases, scripting, batch metadata updates, or other technologies used to manage digital collections. Ability to learn new digital tools, software, and technologies quickly.     To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R312128. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Remote---United-States/Instructional-Design-and-Development-Intern_R312167-1": {
      "title": "Instructional Design and Development Intern",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Description Opportunity: As part of the IDD team, the intern will experience partnering with stakeholders to assess and design solutions aligned with learning outcomes and create instructional content that supports award-winning course design. This position will support and deliver on projects, playing a pivotal role in their success. The intern will work with a team of Instructional Designers, Digital Media Specialists, and Digital Media Producers to determine learning goals and design solutions. Additionally, the intern will experience hands-on what it is like to create, manage, and evaluate courses, curriculum, and deliverables within the scope of the role. A wide degree of creativity and self-motivation is expected.  Responsibilities: Work with members of the IDD team to design and develop engaging, innovative, and effective online course materials with clear strategies and tactics to achieve desired learning outcomes. Create new content and review and revise existing learning content in our Learning Management System. Collaborate with Media Producers and Digital Media Specialists to create interactive online course content. Create adult learning solutions through various instructional design methods.  Leverage adult learning principles, considering the learner experience as well as accessibility, and adhering to ERAU standards of design. Work Eligibility Requirements: Applicants may reside in any U.S. state with the exception of Washington, D.C., Washington, Connecticut, California, New York, New Jersey, Maine, Oregon, Colorado, and Hawaii, due to applicable state and local minimum wage requirements for this position. About us   For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.     Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.     Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.  Compensation: Hourly rate: $15.00-$16.00. Compensation for this internship does not include any fringe benefits such as housing, meal plan, or health and wellness benefits. Qualifications Required qualifications: Applicants must be currently pursuing an undergraduate or graduate degree in Instructional Design, Adult Learning, Instructional Technology, Education, or other related field of study. Remote collaborative style; ability to work both independently and in a team environment. Working knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite. Understanding of adult learning theories and applications. Excellent communication and critical thinking skills. Project management skills. Willingness to learn. Hours: Workload will be 20-30 hours per week. All hours worked must be completed during normal business hours. Application Process: To apply to the IDD Internship Program, candidates should submit their resume, a cover letter describing their goals for the internship, one recommendation letter (preferably from one of the candidate’s professors) and a copy of their academic transcript through the online application portal. As part of your application, please also provide the name, title, and contact information of three professional references. The following criteria will be used to assess all applications: Alignment between student goals and internship program goals Grades Recommendation letter Existing experience Applications are currently being accepted for internship opportunities beginning January 11th. Candidates will be informed about the decision from the committee at least two weeks prior to internship start date. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the  Embry-Riddle Career Site  and search for requisition number R312167. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:  Cover letter  Resume  Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)     Current Embry-Riddle employees:  Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.     Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our  website .     Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact  eraujobs@erau.edu  and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Associate-Director-for-Involvement---Orientation_R312104": {
      "title": "Associate Director for Involvement & Orientation",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity     This position manages a unit that provides programs and events to build community, welcome and orient new students, and support a lively campus culture.   The Associate Director plans and implements New Student Orientation programs and the department’s large-scale signature events such as Homecoming and Blue & Gold Week. In addition, this position supervises the Assistant Director for Campus Activities and a graduate assistant. The Associate Director reports to the Executive Director and is part of a collaborative team of professionals supporting student engagement across a wide range of areas that also include student organizations, student government, fraternity & sorority life, and the Student Union. About us   For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.  Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required. Master’s degree in Student Affairs, Counseling, Higher Ed Administration or related field preferred. A minimum of 2-3 years of full-time experience in higher ed student affairs is required.  Experience coordinating major events, preferably in a university setting, is required. Demonstrated knowledge of best practices and professional standards in the areas of Orientation programming, campus events programming, student development, and student advising. Ability to work evening and weekend hours. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the  Embry-Riddle Career Site  and search for requisition number R312104 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:  Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Business-Analyst_R312045": {
      "title": "Business and Information Analyst, Office of the Registrar",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity Under the guidance of the Associate Registrar for Technology and Compliance, the Business and Information Analyst provides functional expertise and technical support for the Student Administration section of the University’s Student Information System and software solutions used in the department. The position provides testing services for patches, upgrades, and other program changes to the system and technical expertise for implementing and managing software solutions in the department. This position supports academic quality in our teaching and learning environment and participates in department strategic planning meetings as a member of the leadership team. The Business and Information Analyst supports internal technical and reporting needs for leadership and functional areas of the department, and ad-hoc reports for colleagues campus wide. This position works to improve business processes across functional areas by generating reports and queries, analyzing data, troubleshooting system errors, disseminating best practices to keep the student record accurate, and maintaining the comprehensive Production Calendar for the department that keeps staff on task meeting all deadlines. This position works in conjunction with the office’s other Business and Information Analyst to support external technical and reporting needs by serving as a technical/functional student record expert and resource campus wide. Externally they support orientation, academic advising, and faculty ad-hoc reports. This position supports excellence in student services at every opportunity.  This is an in-person position that requires regular on-campus attendance. This role is not eligible for remote or hybrid work. About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Qualifications   Bachelor's degree in business, technology, adult education, or related area. Required: 1-3 years of work-related experience.     To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R312045 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Chair--Department-of-Aeronautical-Science_R312080": {
      "title": "Chair, Department of Aeronautical Science, Daytona Beach Campus",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University’s College of Aviation invites applications for the position of Chair of the Department of Aeronautical Science at the Daytona Beach Campus. The Department Chair provides academic leadership, administrative oversight, and strategic direction for the department. Reporting to the Dean of the College of Aviation, the Chair ensures the quality, integrity, and relevance of departmental programs while supporting the University’s mission, academic goals, and commitment to excellence in aviation education. This position includes a faculty appointment at the rank of Professor or another appropriate academic rank, based on the successful candidate’s qualifications and experience. Responsibilities: The Department Chair will: Provide leadership and direction for the department’s academic programs, faculty, staff, and students. Oversee course scheduling, faculty assignments, faculty evaluations, course documentation, and related academic administrative processes. Manage departmental resources through the University’s budget and salary administration processes. Implement continuous quality improvement and program assessment activities consistent with accreditation requirements. Support student retention initiatives in coordination with the Office of Undergraduate Advising. Oversee appropriate advising activities and maintain accurate student and academic records. Promote academic excellence in teaching, research, and service through faculty mentoring and regular review of course evaluations. Address faculty performance matters in consultation with the Dean and Human Resources, as appropriate. Establish and maintain relationships with professional organizations and aviation industry partners. Ensure that departmental programs provide students with appropriate educational preparation for professional and academic success. Determine and verify appropriate faculty credentials. Recruit, develop, and retain highly qualified faculty who meet University curriculum, scholarship, and instructional standards. Serve on department, college, and campus committees as needed. Perform other duties as assigned by the Dean. The Chair will also maintain an active faculty role, including teaching, scholarship, and service responsibilities consistent with the expectations of the College of Aviation and the University. About us For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries. Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow. Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace. About the department of Aeronautical Science The Department of Aeronautical Science at Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University’s Daytona Beach Campus prepares students for successful careers across the aviation industry through rigorous academics, immersive flight training, and applied learning. The department offers programs in Aeronautical Science, Aeronautics, and Uncrewed and Autonomous Systems, along with related certificates and minors. Our faculty bring extensive experience as airline and military pilots, corporate and test pilots, aerospace professionals, flight safety experts, and aviation researchers. Through strong industry partnerships, hands-on instruction, simulation, research, and mentorship, the department equips students with the technical knowledge, professional judgment, and leadership skills needed to succeed in traditional and emerging aviation careers. Learn more about the Department of Aeronautical Science . Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle! Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26. Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period. Generous Time Off: Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day. Qualifications Required Qualifications Earned doctorate in aeronautical science, aviation, aerospace, or a closely related discipline. Significant academic and professional experience in aviation or aeronautical science. Record of successful teaching, scholarship, and service appropriate for appointment at the professor level. Demonstrated academic leadership or administrative experience, preferably as a department chair, program director, associate dean, or comparable academic administrator. Knowledge of curriculum development, assessment, accreditation, and continuous improvement practices. Experience recruiting, mentoring, evaluating, and developing faculty. Strong communication, interpersonal, organizational, and decision-making skills. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, students, administrators, industry partners, and professional organizations. Preferred Qualifications Experience leading an aviation or aeronautical science program. Knowledge of flight education, aviation operations, aviation safety, or related areas. Experience working with aviation accreditation or regulatory requirements. Established relationships with aviation industry, professional, or governmental organizations. Experience supporting enrollment, student retention, and graduate outcomes. Application process/requirements Review of applications will begin October 1st and will continue until the position has been filled. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R312080 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: Cover letter Full CV Statements of teaching philosophy Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process) Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday. Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website . Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Assistant-Director-of-Health-Services_R312111-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Health Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity     The Assistant Director of Health Services, in alignment with the mission, vision, and strategic priorities of Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University (ERAU) and the Division of Student Affairs, provides high-quality, student-centered customer service that support student well-being and success within the Department of Health services. The Assistant Director, reporting to the Director of Health Services, is responsible for providing direct oversight and operational leadership for the University's Student Medical Response Team (SMRT), which provides evening and weekend emergency medical response to support the campus community. The Assistant Director will coordinate closely with Student Affairs, Risk Management, Campus Safety, Health Services, and local emergency response partners to support effective emergency response and continuity of care. The Assistant Director is also responsible for the development, implementation, and assessment of a comprehensive health promotion and outreach program through Health Services. This includes supervision of the Nutritionist, developing proactive educational initiatives, programs, and partnerships designed to increase student awareness of health and wellness resources, encourage healthy behaviors, and address emerging student health needs. The Assistant Director serves on-call for the Student Medical Response Team (SMRT) and provides leadership and support for emergency response operations as needed. This is a full-time, 12-month, in-person position that requires regular availability during traditional business hours as well as some evenings and weekends based on departmental, outreach, and emergency response needs. About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Qualifications   Bachelor's degree required, with an area of concentration in Healthcare, Nutrition, or Higher Education Current state certification/license as a Paramedic Basic Life Support To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R312111. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/101-Corsair-Hall/Health-and-Well-being-Coordinator_R312115": {
      "title": "Health and Well-being Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University is seeking a Health & Well-Being Coordinator to help shape and advance a culture of health and well-being for faculty and staff across our campuses and remote work environments. This is an exciting opportunity for a creative, collaborative professional who enjoys turning ideas into meaningful programs, connecting employees with valuable resources, and using data and engagement strategies to make a measurable difference. The Health & Well-Being Coordinator will lead the development and delivery of a comprehensive employee well-being strategy encompassing physical, mental, financial, social, and preventive well-being. The position will also help employees better understand and navigate university-sponsored health benefits and resources while partnering with benefit vendors to increase engagement, improve healthcare utilization, and strengthen the overall employee experience. What You’ll Do In this role, you will have the opportunity to: Shape our well-being strategy by leading annual planning, establishing priorities, and developing meaningful measures of success. Create programs employees value across mental health, financial wellness, physical activity, nutrition, preventive care, and social connection. Connect employees with resources by helping faculty and staff understand and effectively use available health benefits, programs, and healthcare resources. Turn data into action by identifying population health trends and opportunities to improve care quality, access, affordability, and employee engagement. Build engagement across our community by developing strategies that reach employees across campuses and remote locations and creating a network of wellness champions. Bring well-being to life through communication by developing clear, actionable content for email, intranet, newsletters, webinars, and other digital channels. Create engaging experiences through wellness challenges, workshops, webinars, campaigns, and other employee-focused events. Build strong partnerships by working closely with university stakeholders and external benefit and wellness partners. Measure our impact by tracking participation, engagement, and program outcomes and translating results into meaningful executive reporting. How to Apply To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number   R312115. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: Cover letter Full CV Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process) About Embry-Riddle For nearly 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense, and technology industries. Today, our faculty, researchers, and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems, and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies, and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow. Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist, or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose, and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace. Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday. Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions—including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment—based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website. Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff. Qualifications Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in health promotion, public health, wellness, human resources, benefits administration, healthcare administration, or a related field. Experience developing, coordinating, or supporting employee wellness, health promotion, benefits, or population health programs. Strong communication and presentation skills, with the ability to translate health and benefits information into clear, engaging, and actionable employee communications. Demonstrated ability to coordinate multiple programs, initiatives, events, and partnerships simultaneously. Strong analytical skills with the ability to use participation, engagement, utilization, and other program data to identify trends and opportunities. Ability to build collaborative relationships with employees, university stakeholders, healthcare partners, and external vendors. Strong organizational skills, initiative, and attention to detail. Preferred Qualifications Experience supporting employee well-being or benefits programs within a large, multi-location organization. Experience working with health plans, wellness vendors, employee assistance programs, or other health and well-being partners. Experience developing wellness campaigns, challenges, workshops, webinars, or employee education programs. Experience analyzing population health, benefits utilization, engagement, or program outcome data. Knowledge of emerging practices and trends in employee health, well-being, and benefits engagement."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Associate-Director-of-Philanthropy--COA_R312123-1": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Philanthropy, COA",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity       Reporting to the Senior Executive Director of Philanthropy for Aviation, the Associate Director of Philanthropy supports development efforts for the College of Aviation in Daytona Beach. In close collaboration with the Senior Executive Director, this position helps execute philanthropic strategies that strengthen the University’s fundraising capacity and advance aviation-focused programs and initiatives. The Associate Director engages donors, alumni, industry partners, and campus stakeholders; coordinates events and campus visits; supports grant development; maintains accurate donor records; and advances annual fund and other philanthropic priorities. The successful candidate is creative, self-motivated, high-energy, detail-oriented, and an outstanding communicator who can qualify and cultivate prospects for solicitation or referral to other gift officers. Key Responsibilities Solicitation Strategy: Develop and execute a comprehensive plan to support the College’s financial objectives, with an annual fundraising goal starting at $100,000. Donor Relations: Cultivate and maintain relationships with current and prospective donors through effective communication, engagement, and follow-through that foster long-term support. Event Coordination: Plan and manage small college events and campus tours, and execute sponsorship benefits in accordance with applicable agreements. Grant Writing: Identify grant opportunities, prepare proposals, and manage the application process to support annual fundraising goals. Database Management: Maintain accurate and timely donor and prospect records in the University’s customer relationship management (CRM) system. College Liaison: Serve as a liaison for the College of Aviation and coordinate with internal departments to support philanthropic initiatives and priorities. Essential Job Functions, Duties, and Accountabilities Prospect Qualification, Referral, and Solicitation - Annual Fund Level Manage an assigned portfolio of approximately 125 prospects for qualification related to major gifts, the annual fund, College Philanthropy Councils, affinity groups, and other initiatives. Work within a fast-paced cadence of outreach, cultivation, solicitation, and referral through email, telephone, and videoconference. Success will be measured by the volume and quality of prospects assessed, qualified, referred, and solicited. Research and identify grant opportunities, prepare compelling proposals, and manage the application process to secure foundation support. Donor Stewardship Work alongside the Senior Director of Stewardship to ensure College of Aviation donors receive exceptional stewardship commensurate with their level of giving, with the goal of increasing and renewing philanthropic support. Coordinate with Financial Aid to ensure College scholarships are awarded effectively and efficiently and that donors receive timely information about scholarship recipients. Coordinate with appropriate departments to execute sponsorship benefits, including press releases, signage, logo placement, and other deliverables outlined in sponsorship agreements. Unit Liaison and Support Serve as the PAE liaison for the College of Aviation and coordinate philanthropic marketing and communications, external communications, Career Services, Corporate Relations, and other partners as requested by the Senior Executive Director of Philanthropy for Aviation. Collaborate with the PAE Marketing and Communications team to create program and proposal materials for donor and prospect visits. Coordinate campus visits for industry partners, donors, and prospective donors. Work with Alumni Engagement and other PAE partners to facilitate giving campaigns, including faculty and staff campaigns and crowdfunding initiatives, as requested.     About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Qualifications     • Bachelor’s degree. • At least three years of fundraising experience within higher education or a nonprofit organization. • Demonstrated ability to identify, cultivate, solicit, and steward donors at the annual fund level. • Strong writing, presentation, and interpersonal communication skills. • Ability to work collaboratively across departments with consistent and robust follow-through. • Strong character and demonstrated integrity, care, honesty, and loyalty to the institution. • Ability to develop proficiency with the University’s CRM software and generate and interpret prospect reports. • Ability to prioritize and manage multiple tasks, changing priorities, and deadlines effectively. • Ability to adapt and remain resilient when confronted with challenges or changing priorities. • Ability to compile expense reports and appropriately plan and execute social engagement activities. • Ability to manage sensitive and confidential information. • Willingness to work occasional evenings and weekends. • Valid driver’s license and the ability to drive safely and effectively. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R312123 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Senior-Executive-Director-of-Philanthropy--College-of-Aviation_R312124": {
      "title": "Senior Executive Director of Philanthropy, College of Aviation",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity     Since its inception, Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University has remained a global leader in aerospace education, innovation, and research. Founded in 1926, the University is preparing to celebrate a century of achievement while shaping the future of aviation and aerospace. As Embry-Riddle launches its Centennial Campaign, Imagine What’s Next, the Office of Philanthropy and Alumni Engagement seeks a dynamic and seasoned fundraiser to serve as Senior Executive Director of Philanthropy for the College of Aviation at the Daytona Beach campus. Reporting to the Vice President for Philanthropy and Alumni Engagement and collaborating closely with the Dean of the College of Aviation, this leader will chart the course for fundraising success by cultivating relationships with alumni, foundations, corporate partners, and other key constituents. The role offers an opportunity to advance aerospace education, champion innovation, and leave a lasting impact on the University’s future. Key Responsibilities • Major Gifts: Manage an assigned portfolio of individual, corporate, and foundation prospects through discovery, qualification, cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship, with a focus on closing more than $3 million annually in philanthropic support. Engage donors through correspondence, calls, events, and extensive face-to-face visits. Track solicitation and stewardship progress in Salesforce in accordance with University prospect management guidelines. Develop and implement long-term strategies for each prospect and collaborate with division colleagues to achieve unit and institutional goals. • Unit Liaison: Coordinate and participate in development activities within the College of Aviation and attend the Dean’s leadership meetings to understand the College’s needs, challenges, and opportunities. Coordinate with central advancement on annual giving, advancement communications, data acquisition, planned giving, donor relations, and donor impact reporting. Advise the Dean on philanthropic policies, practices, schedules, strategies, and best practices. Build effective relationships with administrators, faculty, and staff and engage them in fundraising efforts. • Collaboration and Communication: Translate complex scientific concepts and programs into compelling, donor-friendly language for proposals and outreach. Prepare fundraising communications, foundation reports, faculty updates, acknowledgment letters, and other materials. Monitor University outreach events for major gift leads and develop meaningful donor and prospect events that showcase opportunities for support. • Staff Management: Lead and manage the Director of Philanthropy and Associate Director of Philanthropy for the College of Aviation. Support professional development through inclusive, transparent, and empowering leadership. Participate in regular staff and frontline fundraiser meetings to coordinate development and alumni relations activities, and serve on committees as requested. • Other Duties: Perform other duties as assigned and appropriate to the position’s rank and the University’s mission. About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.       Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.       Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.       Generous Time Off:   Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage:   Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions:   ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave:   Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Qualifications   • Bachelor’s degree required; foreign equivalent or higher accepted. • Ten years of full-time fundraising experience in higher education, a complex healthcare system, or a large nonprofit organization. • Proven record of success cultivating, soliciting, and closing major gifts of $100,000 or more from individual donors. • Experience managing numerous priorities and a broad portfolio of donor or client relationships. • Experience with Salesforce or a comparable donor relationship management application. Preferred Qualifications   • Master’s degree. • Additional fundraising experience in higher education, a large nonprofit organization, or a healthcare institution. • Experience working in an academic or medical center. • Experience managing volunteers or an advisory board. • Comfort working with high-net-worth individuals and maintaining confidential information. • Basic knowledge of planned giving vehicles and techniques. • Experience developing a new donor constituency. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the   Embry-Riddle Career Site   and search for requisition number R312124 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter   Resume   Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)       Current Embry-Riddle employees:   Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.       Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our   website .       Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact   eraujobs@erau.edu   and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
