    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Director---Corporate-Philanthropy_R312238": {
      "title": "Director – Corporate Philanthropy",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-30\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nJob Description Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University’s Office of Philanthropy and Alumni Engagement (PAE) seeks an accomplished and entrepreneurial advancement professional to serve as Director, Corporate Philanthropy. Reporting to the Senior Executive Director of Corporate Philanthropy and Foundation Relations, the Director will manage and grow a portfolio of corporate partners whose interests align with the University’s priorities in aviation, aerospace, space, engineering, technology, business, workforce development, and student success. The Director will identify, cultivate, solicit, and steward relationships that generate philanthropic gifts, corporate grants, sponsorships, in-kind support, and other strategic investments. Working closely with career services and academic units, the Director will connect corporate interests with University priorities and develop comprehensive, mutually beneficial partnerships with key companies. The Director will manage approximately 40 to 60 active corporate prospects, build a strong and sustainable pipeline, and secure $1 million or more annually in philanthropic support once the portfolio is fully established. Specifically, the Director will: Manage a portfolio of approximately 40 to 60 active corporate prospects and partners through all stages of identification, qualification, cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship. Develop and execute written engagement and solicitation strategies for assigned companies, with clear objectives, next steps, timelines, and internal partners. Conduct substantive meetings with corporate executives, corporate foundation leaders, alumni, and other decision-makers to understand company priorities and identify areas of mutual interest. Prepare and execute corporate campus visits, briefings, solicitations, and stewardship activities involving University leaders and appropriate colleagues. Develop concept papers, proposals, sponsorship packages, executive briefings, correspondence, and other materials in partnership with faculty, program leaders, PAE communications, and advancement colleagues. Coordinate proposal development timelines, budgets, approvals, and supporting documentation to ensure accurate and timely submissions. Partner with Donor Relations, Advancement Services, communications staff, and University program leaders to provide timely acknowledgment, reporting, recognition, and stewardship for corporate partners. Represent the University at various cultivation and fundraising events, working in tandem with the Senior Executive Director of Corporate Philanthropy and Foundation Relations. Track progress and results in Salesforce, the University’s database, following ERAU’s prospect management guidelines. About us    For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.     Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.     Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.       Generous Time Off: Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave: Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution. A minimum of five years of progressively responsible experience in corporate relations, institutional advancement, major gifts, strategic partnerships, business development, consultative sales, or a related field. Demonstrated success developing complex institutional or corporate relationships and moving opportunities from identification through commitment. Demonstrated experience securing significant philanthropic gifts, grants, sponsorships, partnerships, or comparable revenue-producing commitments. Experience using Salesforce or a comparable advancement CRM. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree or higher. Record of securing six-figure or larger corporate gifts, grants, sponsorships, or strategic partnerships. Experience working with aviation, aerospace, space, engineering, technology, business, workforce development, or related industries. Experience developing proposals for complex academic, research, or student-success initiatives. Essential Job Functions, Duties, or Accountabilities: Corporate portfolio management and fundraising. Comprehensive corporate partnership development and University coordination. Proposal development, stewardship, and communications. Planning, reporting, events, and team contribution. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R312238. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter  Resume  Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)     Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.     Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website .     Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Tenure-Track-Assistant-Professor-of-Aeronautical-Sciences--Daytona-Beach-Campus_R312192": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor of Aeronautical Sciences, Daytona Beach Campus",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity The Aeronautical Science Department in the College of Aviation (COA) at Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University—Daytona Beach invites applications for a Tenure-Track 9-month appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor. The qualified candidate will teach courses held in the Department of Aeronautical Science for both the Aeronautical Science and Aeronautics undergraduate degree programs. They will also demonstrate an active or promising research agenda in areas of study consistent with flight operations or other aviation related subjects. Excellence in teaching and the growth of a well-developed research portfolio are our top priority. Other priorities include service to the university and a strong commitment to student mentorship. The qualified candidate will have a broad base of knowledge and experience in the operation of large-transport category aircraft or high performance aircraft used in commercial aircraft transportation. Courseware may include requisite material based in large transport category flight operations, crew resource management, aviation safety, domestic and international navigation, aircraft systems, and other content areas brought forth through course/department expansion. The appropriate candidate will hold an earned doctorate in a related field from an accredited institution and will possess a strong interest in advancing aviation education and research through a strong record of publishing and grant procurement. About us For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries. Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow. Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace. Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle! Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26. Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period. Qualifications Required Education: Doctoral degree in Aeronautical Science or related field and FAA Licensure commensurate with position requirements. Application process/requirements Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R312192 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: Cover letter Full CV Statements of teaching philosophy Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process) Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday. Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website . Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Media-Producer_R312256": {
      "title": "Media Producer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity   Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University – Worldwide is seeking a creative and detail-oriented Media Producer to join the Academic Innovation – Learning Design & Technology team. This role is responsible for planning, producing, and delivering high-quality photo, video, and motion graphics that support online courses and university initiatives. The Media Producer collaborates with faculty, leadership, and cross-functional teams to create engaging digital content that enhances the student learning experience. This position also plays a key role in live event production, including commencement ceremonies and university events. This is an excellent opportunity for a media professional who thrives in a fast-paced, collaborative environment and is passionate about storytelling, innovation, and visual excellence. Key Responsibilities Produce high-quality video, photo, and digital media content for online courses and university initiatives Plan, shoot, edit, and deliver multimedia projects using industry-standard tools and technologies Collaborate with stakeholders to define project scope, timelines, and deliverables Manage multiple projects simultaneously while meeting deadlines and maintaining quality standards Provide guidance and coaching to stakeholders on best practices for media creation and instructional design Develop scripts, storyboards, and creative concepts aligned with project goals Ensure all media content meets accessibility standards, including Section 508 compliance Support live production events, including setup, camera operation, lighting, audio, and streaming technology Maintain organized digital asset libraries and project files Continuously improve workflows, adopt new technologies, and contribute to team innovation    About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.     Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.     Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.       Generous Time Off: Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave: Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.       Compensation   The annual salary range for this position is $51,857 . The final offer will consider the candidate’s skills, qualifications, and experience, along with applicable state regulations, internal equity, and business needs, and may fall outside of the stated range.     Qualifications Required Education and Qualifications:   Bachelor’s degree in Video Production, Broadcasting, Digital Media, or a related field 1–3 years of experience in media production, creative services, or a related field Proficiency with video production equipment, including cameras, lighting, and audio gear Experience with video editing software such as Adobe Premiere Pro Ability to capture high-quality video and photography using cinema and mirrorless cameras Strong understanding of lighting techniques and audio recording best practices Experience managing multiple projects and working within deadlines Strong communication, collaboration, and interpersonal skills Ability to accept feedback and work effectively in a team environment Knowledge of accessibility standards and brand consistency practices Willingness to work flexible hours, including evenings or weekends for events Ability to lift and transport media equipment and work in various production environments Application process/requirements   To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the  Embry-Riddle Career Site  and search for requisition number  R312256 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:  Cover letter  Full Resume  Portfolio Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)     Current Embry-Riddle employees:  Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.     Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our  website .    Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
