    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Aeronautical-Science--NTT---Daytona-Beach-Campus_R312266": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Aeronautical Science (NTT), Daytona Beach Campus",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-12\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity The Aeronautical Science Department in the College of Aviation (COA) at Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University—Daytona Beach invites applications for a non-tenure track position at the rank of Assistant/Associate Professor to teach in the Aeronautical Science and Aeronautics undergraduate programs. Both degree programs are housed in the Aeronautical Science Department. Teaching excellence is our top priority along with applied research in aviation related areas. Key to our mission is providing effective mentoring and advising to our students as they prepare to enter the industry. All programs housed in the AS department are accredited by the Aviation Accreditation Board International (AABI).   This position requires a broad base of knowledge and experience gained through the operation of various aircraft. Teaching areas may include requisite material for private, instrument, and commercial ground schools, large transport category operations, crew resource management, aviation safety, domestic and international navigation, aircraft systems, simulated operations, and other content areas brought forth through course/department expansion. In addition to teaching responsibilities, duties will include curriculum development and committee participation on Department and University levels. The candidate will also have a strong interest in pursuing or supporting scholarship and professional activities appropriate to advancing aviation education and aviation interests in the industry.   About the Aeronautical Science) Department and the College of Aviation (COA)  The Aeronautical Science (AS) Department hosts the largest degree program for professional pilots in the world and is one of the largest departments on the Daytona Beach Campus. It houses three undergraduate degree programs focusing on professional aviation, which include the Bachelor of Science in Aeronautical Science, Bachelor of Science in Aeronautics and Bachelor of Science in Uncrewed Aircraft Systems. All programs in the AS department are accredited by the Aviation Accreditation Board International (AABI).   The College of Aviation is the global leader in aviation and aerospace education and research and curriculum innovation.  We are renowned for outstanding people and programs and the impact of our work. The college is guided by concern for ethical and responsible behavior nested in a culture of safety and professionalism.  We believe a vibrant future for aviation and aerospace rests in the knowledge, skills, attitudes, and abilities of our graduates.    About us For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.   Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.   Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle! Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26. Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period. Qualifications Required Education and Qualifications Master’s degree in Aeronautical Science or related field and FAA Licensure commensurate with position requirements.   Application process/requirements Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.   To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R312266 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: Cover letter Full CV Statements of teaching philosophy Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)   Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.   Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website .   Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/259-Boeing-Center-for-Aviation--Aerospace-Safety/Vice-President-of-Professional-Education_R312281": {
      "title": "Vice President of Professional Education",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-12\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nJob Description Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University is seeking a dynamic, entrepreneurial and results-oriented leader to serve as its Vice President of Professional Education . Reporting directly to the Senior Vice President for Academic Affairs and Provost , this position will serve as the university's senior executive and single point of accountability for non-credit professional, executive, corporate and workforce education. The Vice President will lead the development of a coordinated, enterprise-wide professional education portfolio, positioning Embry-Riddle as the global leader in aviation and aerospace professional education and the preferred first call for companies, governments and individuals seeking high-value education and training. This executive will set university-wide strategy for professional education offerings, determining which programs and products to develop, scale, combine, stack, subsidize or retire. The Vice President will bring greater coordination to professional education across the university, reduce internal competition, strengthen the Embry-Riddle brand and ensure the portfolio responds to evolving industry and workforce needs. Working across Embry-Riddle's campuses in Daytona Beach, Prescott, Worldwide and Asia, the Vice President will integrate market intelligence, business development, pricing, marketing, digital presence, customer intake, financial management and performance measurement to create an exceptional customer experience and a clear value proposition tied to outcomes and return on investment. This is an opportunity for an accomplished leader to build and shape a highly visible, growth-oriented professional education enterprise backed by the expertise, reputation and global reach of Embry-Riddle. Key Responsibilities Strategic Program Development and Leadership Develop and execute a growth strategy for Embry-Riddle's professional education portfolio, including certificate programs, global executive workshops, high-impact in-person programs, micro-credentials, digital badges and on-demand learning pathways. Market Development, Sales and Partnerships Build a disciplined U.S. and global consultative sales approach and develop lasting relationships with corporations, government organizations, associations and individual learners. Identify new markets, cultivate strategic partnerships and expand Embry-Riddle's position as a trusted provider of professional and workforce education. Portfolio and Product Leadership Use market intelligence, competitive analysis, enrollment results and customer feedback to guide program development, launches, renewals, stackability, consolidation and retirement across the university's professional education portfolio. Delivery and Academic Partnerships Coordinate asynchronous, synchronous, hybrid, online, on-site and campus-based delivery. Partner across Embry-Riddle to leverage academic expertise, online production capabilities, faculty, external practitioners and university resources while determining the optimal campus, unit or partner for each offering. Financial and Operational Leadership Provide executive oversight of pricing, contracting, budgets, financial models, registration, CRM and program delivery operations. Manage strategic investments in new program launches, market development, distinctive expertise and pilot initiatives while ensuring financial sustainability. Customer Experience, Marketing and Digital Presence Create a seamless experience for professional education customers through a unified digital presence, customer intake process, point of contact, messaging, marketing, outreach, registration, CRM and post-program engagement. Quality, Talent and Organizational Leadership Establish expectations for quality, impact and return on investment. Monitor performance, drive continuous improvement and develop effective approaches for engaging and compensating faculty, staff, designers, course leaders and external experts. The Vice President will directly lead the professional education team while providing matrixed leadership across faculty, staff, subject-matter experts, instructional designers, marketing and sales professionals, and campus and college partners contributing to university-wide offerings. The role will also represent Embry-Riddle at industry conferences, trade shows, government forums and executive events and remain closely attuned to workforce, regulatory, competitive and technology trends affecting the future of professional education. Travel and Schedule This position is based in Daytona Beach, Florida and typically follows standard business hours, Monday through Friday. Because Embry-Riddle's professional education enterprise serves customers and partners across multiple time zones, flexibility will be required, including occasional evening or weekend commitments associated with executive engagement, program delivery and international coordination. Domestic and international travel is expected to average approximately 20–30% and may include customer and partner visits, business development activities, conferences, program launches and coordination across Embry-Riddle campuses and global locations. About Us For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries. Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow. Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace. Employee Benefits Generous Time Off: Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day. Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26. Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution, with no vesting period. Personal Leave: Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year. Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday. Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website. Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff. To preserve the integrity and authenticity of our hiring process, candidates are expected to participate without AI-assisted coaching, real-time response generation, or recording during interviews or assessments. Embry-Riddle does not use AI to automatically screen, rank, or select candidates. Qualifications Required Qualifications Master's degree in business, education, aviation/aerospace, engineering, workforce development or a related field. 10 or more years of progressive leadership experience, including substantial responsibility within professional, corporate, executive or workforce education. Demonstrated experience with consultative sales, strategic partnerships and enterprise contracts. Experience with pricing, contracting, P&L management, budgeting, marketing, customer acquisition and analytics. Experience overseeing multimodal delivery models and working within international or global operations. Demonstrated ability to govern a broad portfolio, align distributed stakeholders and make enterprise-level decisions. Ability to lead effectively within a complex, matrixed environment and navigate competing priorities and interests. Ability to credibly represent Embry-Riddle with corporate executives, government officials, faculty, external experts and prospective learners. Exceptional executive presence, judgment, resilience, communication and relationship-building skills. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate or MBA. Relevant professional or industry credentials. Experience developing or scaling professional education, executive education, workforce development or similar revenue-generating educational enterprises."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Assistant-Director-of-Student-Financial-Services_R312277": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Student Financial Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity      The Assistant Director of Student Financial Services provides leadership and operational oversight for Student Financial Services (SFS) staff and functions, including student accounts, billing, education benefits, training, compliance, and customer service. This role serves as a key leader within SFS, supporting the accuracy, consistency, and continuous improvement of departmental operations while ensuring compliance with university policies, federal and state regulations, and established business practices. The Assistant Director will lead and develop staff, provide guidance on complex student account and customer service matters, review and analyze departmental reports and transactions, and ensure the consistent application of policies and procedures across SFS operations. The position serves as an escalation point for complex account issues and independently researches discrepancies, determines appropriate resolutions, and recommends corrective actions. This position will also lead departmental initiatives focused on process improvement, operational effectiveness, and customer service. The Assistant Director analyzes performance data, identifies trends and areas of concern, prepares reports and recommendations for leadership, and supports audits and compliance activities. The successful candidate will collaborate with internal departments, campus partners, students, families, and external organizations to promote consistent practices and a high level of service. This role requires strong leadership, analytical, communication, problem-solving, and decision-making skills, as well as the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment.    About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.     Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.     Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.       Generous Time Off: Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave: Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.      Qualifications Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Business, Management, Accounting, Finance, or a related field, or equivalent combination of education and experience. Three to five years of related professional experience, preferably in accounting or finance. Strong analytical, problem-solving, critical-thinking, and decision-making skills. Experience managing multiple priorities, projects, and deadlines while maintaining accuracy and attention to detail. Excellent verbal and written communication and interpersonal skills. Strong customer service orientation and the ability to effectively resolve complex customer issues. Demonstrated ability to lead, train, develop, and support staff. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with diverse internal and external constituents. Ability to work independently, exercise sound judgment, and make informed decisions with limited supervision. Ability to maintain a high level of confidentiality and appropriately handle sensitive information. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite, particularly Microsoft Excel. Strong organizational skills and the ability to coordinate multiple responsibilities simultaneously. Ability to adapt to new ideas, processes, technologies, and organizational change. Demonstrated ability to manage employee relations, work priorities, and departmental projects. Preferred Qualifications: Prior leadership experience in student financial services, student accounts, billing, accounts receivable, or collections. Experience working in a higher education environment. Experience with Campus Solutions and TouchNet. Experience with student account reconciliation, billing, payment plans, refunds, collections, write-offs, or account adjustments. Knowledge of federal and state regulations applicable to student financial services. Experience with education benefits or Veterans Affairs-related account processes. Experience developing and implementing business process improvements. Experience preparing operational reports, analyzing data, conducting audits, and identifying process efficiencies.    To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R31227 7. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:  Cover letter  Resume  Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)     Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.     Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website .     Embry-Riddle does not accept unsolicited assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. Agencies interested in partnering with the University should contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not contact hiring managers or other University employees directly.   To preserve the integrity and authenticity of our hiring process, candidates are expected to participate without AI-assisted coaching, real-time response generation, or recording during interviews or assessments. Embry-Riddle does not use AI to automatically screen, rank, or select candidates."
