    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Prescott-AZ/Facilities-Systems-Manager_R312322": {
      "title": "Facilities Systems Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-16\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity      Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University is seeking a detail-oriented and customer-focused Facilities Systems Manager to join the Facilities Management team at our Prescott, Arizona campus. This position manages the university’s Integrated Workplace Management System (IWMS), AssetWorks, including AiM and GO, to support facilities operations, work order management, preventive maintenance, asset tracking, and reporting. The Facilities System Manager serves as the primary point of contact for Facilities personnel and Information Technology regarding the IWMS. Responsibilities include maintaining system accuracy, coordinating preventive maintenance processes, managing service requests, generating operational and utility reports, tracking labor and related costs, and supporting asset condition assessments and capital renewal planning. This position also oversees Service Center operations, ensuring maintenance requests are accurately entered, tracked, and dispatched while maintaining a high standard of customer service. The successful candidate will provide system training, coordinate software updates and troubleshooting, support space management data, and supervise Service Center staff and student employees. The ideal candidate is proactive, organized, and comfortable managing multiple priorities while collaborating with facilities personnel, IT, vendors, and campus stakeholders to improve operational efficiency and support the effective delivery of university facilities services.   About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.     Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.     Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.       Generous Time Off: Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave: Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Required Qualifications: Associate degree or completion of a postsecondary program of at least 18 months, preferably in Business Administration or a related field. One to three years of related work experience in database management, customer service, or a related area. Two years of experience with Facilities Management Integrated Workplace Management Systems (IWMS) or Computerized Maintenance Management Systems (CMMS) may substitute for the associate degree requirement. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, business software, and IWMS applications. Strong attention to detail and commitment to maintaining accurate records and system data. Ability to work independently, take initiative, and manage responsibilities within established deadlines. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated commitment to providing excellent customer service. Ability to manage multiple tasks, analyze information, follow instructions, and exercise sound judgment. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with colleagues, customers, and other stakeholders. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with AssetWorks AiM, GO, or comparable IWMS/CMMS platforms. Experience supporting facilities operations, work order management, preventive maintenance, asset inventory, or service desk operations. Experience generating operational reports, tracking utility usage and billing, or managing timekeeping and labor-related data. Experience providing system training, troubleshooting application issues, and coordinating software updates with IT teams or vendors. Experience supervising staff or student employees. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R312322 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:  Cover letter  Resume  Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)     Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.     Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website .     Embry-Riddle does not accept unsolicited assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. Agencies interested in partnering with the University should contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not contact hiring managers or other University employees directly. To preserve the integrity and authenticity of our hiring process, candidates are expected to participate without AI-assisted coaching, real-time response generation, or recording during interviews or assessments. Embry-Riddle does not use AI to automatically screen, rank, or select candidates."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Remote---United-States/Tenure-Track-Assistant-Associate-Professor--Aviation-Commercial-Management--Worldwide-Campus--Remote-Role-_R312255": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant/Associate Professor, Aviation Commercial Management, Worldwide Campus (Remote Role)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-16\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity The College of Business (COB) at Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University Worldwide (ERAU-W) is seeking a Full Time Tenure-Track Faculty to join the COB and Department of Business Administration as Assistant/Associate Professor in Aviation Commercial Management. This is a remote position and will require an at home office. The successful candidate will teach graduate and undergraduate commercial management courses. The typical teaching load is 24 credit hours per academic year, which extends from 1 August to 31 May. The role represents a great opportunity to work alongside dedicated colleagues committed to making a difference to industry and features key lifestyle benefits such as the opportunity to work at home, paid holidays in addition to summer release (June-July off), exceptional health benefits, generous retirement contributions and Embry-Riddle tuition waivers for faculty and their family members. Faculty will teach with innovative academic technologies and delivery platforms almost entirely online. Courses reside within the College of Business and have a strong business and commercial aviation focus. Responsibilities: Teach primarily commercial aviation business courses Develop, maintain, and assess courses, particularly those that feature on the College’s M.S. Airline and Airport and Air Mobility-related degree programs Develop and update curricula as needed Demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching, staying current in the profession, and providing service to the department, college, university, and profession Limited travel for meetings and conferences will be required About the College of Business Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University (ERAU) is the world’s largest, fully accredited university specializing in aviation, aerospace, and related fields. ERAU is a nonprofit, independent institution offering more than 80 baccalaureate, master’s, and Ph.D. degree programs. The Worldwide campus has an enrollment of over 20,500 students. Courses are delivered online via Canvas, synchronously via Zoom, and face-to-face around the globe in the United States, Europe, Asia, South America, and the Middle East. Over the last decade Embry-Riddle Worldwide has earned high rankings as one of the Best Online Bachelors programs from US News and World Report often ranked in the top 5. In 2026, the ranking was 11. The Worldwide College of Business is a highly entrepreneurial organization with a broad reach in the aviation industry. COB values and supports activities that are directed at solving business challenges, especially in the broader aviation sector. The college offers two Associate’s Degrees (Aviation Business Administration and Technical Management), six Bachelor’s degrees (Aviation Business Administration, Business Analytics, Leadership, Logistics and Supply Chain Management, Project Management and Technical Management), and eight Master’s degrees (Business Administration in Aviation, Engineering Management, Information Security & Assurance, Leadership, Logistics and Supply Chain Management, Management, Management Information Systems, and Project Management). Virtually all COB programs have industry affiliations, including with ISM, PMI, SAP, SAS, ASEM, RAeS and others. Departments in the COB are Business Administration, Decision Sciences and Analytics, and Management. The successful candidate would be assigned to the Department of Management (DM). The DM houses the Associate in Technical Management, Bachelor of Science in Technical Management, Masters in Management, Masters in Leadership, Masters in Airline Management, and Masters in Airport and Air Mobility Management. A mixture of undergraduate minors, majors, professional education, and graduate certificates are also managed by the DM. Embry-Riddle: Celebrating 100 Years of Leadership in Aviation and Aerospace   As Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University marks its Centennial, we proudly celebrate 100 years of advancing the future of flight and aerospace education. With vibrant residential campuses in Daytona Beach, FL, and Prescott, AZ — and a Worldwide network spanning   nearly 120   global locations — Embry-Riddle stands as the world’s largest aviation and aerospace university.   For a century, we have led innovation in STEM education, serving more than 30,000 students around the globe. Our   cutting-edge   programs in Applied Science, Aviation, Business, Technology, Engineering, Safety, Security, and Space empower the next generation of leaders to shape the future of flight, exploration, and discovery.   As we launch our next century, we   remain   committed to excellence, innovation, and preparing graduates who will transform industries and redefine what is possible.   Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle!    Generous Time Off: Enjoy 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year’s Day. Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26. Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period. Qualifications Required Education and Qualifications: At Assistant level a relevant Masters from an accredited institution is required, while a doctorate is preferred. At Associate level a doctorate is required. Preferred candidates will have commercial management experience from the airline, airport or related commercial aviation supplier sector. Candidates with direct and demonstrable knowledge in the management of customer experience, brand and marketing strategies, revenue generation and cost management, sales and distribution, route and network evaluations and planning, or partnerships and sponsorship strategies are particularly encouraged to apply. The successful candidate should show excellence in teaching and demonstrate strong research potential/pipeline at the Assistant level and through publications and an ongoing pipeline at Associate level, that would include working papers or papers under review. Candidates must have excellent teaching evaluations in related fields. Experience in higher education teaching (web-based courses preferred), participation in university committees, industry boards or related community organizations, participation in state/national professional organizations, and past successful professional experience with diverse groups. Strong written and communication skills A clearly defined teaching philosophy Demonstrated ability to engage and mentor students from diverse backgrounds (in a remote setting preferred) Willingness to travel as necessary for the position (approximately 5-10%) Experience in course design and development for online course delivery is preferred Experience with online learning management systems is preferred Candidates should be collegial professionals passionate about teaching and the aviation industry, treating them both as a hobby and a profession, and have a keen interest in all aspects of aviation business. The candidate will adhere to the COB-W values of: (a) integrity, (b) collaboration/collegiality, (c) student- centricity, (d) respect, and (e) innovation. Personal attributes: The ideal candidate is a dynamic team player who values collaboration and solution-focused approaches as well as possessing strong listening skills, an open and positive mindset, flexibility to adapt to rapid changes, prioritizes effectively even when resources are scarce, is adept at juggling multiple responsibilities simultaneously, welcomes constructive feedback and is committed to continuous improvement and personal growth. Application process/requirements Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. The start date will be based off the candidate's availability. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R312255 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: A cover letter describing your interest in the position and qualifications for the role A current curriculum vitae Contact information for three professional references Summary of evidence of teaching effectiveness (i.e., course evaluations, teaching portfolio, etc.) and industry engagement/involvement For Associate Professor level a statement of research contributions to date and future aspirations (up to a page in length) Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday. Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website . Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Research-Scientist_R311732": {
      "title": "Research Scientist, Department of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science, Daytona Beach Campus",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-15\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity The Department of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science (EECS) at Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University invites applications for a Research Scientist position on the Daytona Beach Campus. The successful candidate will conduct independent and collaborative research in wireless communications, sensing systems, and related technologies while supporting the department's growing portfolio of externally sponsored research. The Research Scientist will contribute to the development and execution of federally and industry funded research projects, publish scholarly work, mentor undergraduate and graduate student researchers, and collaborate with faculty, industry partners, and government agencies to advance innovative research initiatives. This position offers an exciting opportunity to work in a multidisciplinary research environment focused on next-generation communications, sensing technologies, autonomy, cybersecurity, and intelligent systems. Primary Responsibilities Conduct independent and collaborative research in wireless communications, sensing systems, and related technical areas. Develop, execute, and manage sponsored research projects. Contribute to the preparation of competitive research proposals for federal agencies, industry, and other sponsors. Design, implement, and evaluate scientific experiments, simulations, and analytical models. Publish research findings in high-quality peer-reviewed journals and present results at national and international conferences. Mentor undergraduate and graduate student researchers. Collaborate with faculty across the university as well as external academic, government, and industry partners. Assist in developing and maintaining research laboratories and experimental capabilities. Support the department's strategic research initiatives and technology transition activities. About us For nearly 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries. Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow. Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace. Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle! Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26. Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period. Generous Time Off: Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day. Qualifications Required Education Ph.D. or other doctorate-level equivalent in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or a closely related field. Required Experience Three to five (3–5) years of related professional research experience. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrated research experience and scholarly accomplishments in a relevant technical area. Strong analytical, problem-solving, written, and verbal communication skills. Experience with scientific programming, modeling, simulation, or experimental research methodologies. Experience participating in externally sponsored research projects. Record of peer-reviewed publications and technical presentations. Experience mentoring undergraduate, graduate, or junior researchers. Ability to contribute to proposal development and collaborative multidisciplinary research initiatives. Preferred Qualifications Wireless communications and networking RF systems and signal processing Radar and sensing systems Software-defined radio AI/ML applications for communications and sensing Embedded systems and edge computing Autonomous systems and intelligent sensing Cyber-physical systems Experience working with federal research sponsors such as NSF, DoD, NASA, FAA, DOE, or related agencies is desirable. Application process/requirements Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R311732 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: Cover letter Full CV Statements of teaching philosophy Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process) Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.   Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website .   Embry-Riddle does not accept unsolicited assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. Agencies interested in partnering with the University should contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not contact hiring managers or other University employees directly.   To preserve the integrity and authenticity of our hiring process, candidates are expected to participate without AI-assisted coaching, real-time response generation, or recording during interviews or assessments. Embry-Riddle does not use AI to automatically screen, rank, or select candidates."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Tenure-Track-Tenured-Faculty--Systems-Engineering--Daytona-Beach-Campus_R312103": {
      "title": "Tenure Track/Tenured Faculty, Systems Engineering, Daytona Beach Campus",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-15\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity The Department of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science (EECS) in the College of Engineering at Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University’s Daytona Beach Campus invites applications for a tenured or tenure-track faculty position in Systems Engineering at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor.   The successful candidate will join a growing systems engineering community supporting Bachelor of Science and Master of Science programs in Systems Engineering, as well as a systems-focused pathway within the Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering and Computer Science. The faculty member will have opportunities to contribute to the continued development of the department’s academic programs, research initiatives, and student opportunities.   The department maintains strong connections to the systems engineering profession through faculty membership in the INCOSE Academic Council, leadership roles at leading systems engineering technical conferences, and service on the INRESCOS advisory board. Recent initiatives have further strengthened the student experience, including the launch of a student INCOSE club, expanded access to Cameo modeling resources, and INCOSE Academic Equivalency recognition supporting the Associate Systems Engineering Professional (ASEP) certification pathway.   The successful candidate will be expected to contribute to the department’s research mission, deliver student-centered instruction, mentor undergraduate and graduate students, and participate in service activities. Applicants should share the department’s commitment to an inclusive, collegial, and collaborative academic environment.   About the Department of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science (EECS) EECS is home to 24 faculty members and multiple degrees: the  Ph.D. degree in Electrical Engineering and Computer Science ; M.S. degrees in  Cybersecurity Engineering ,  Electrical and Computer Engineering ,  Software Engineering ,  Systems Engineering , and  Unmanned and Autonomous Systems Engineering ; and B.S. degrees in  Systems Engineering , Computer Engineering ,  Computer Science ,  Electrical Engineering , and  Software Engineering . The department offers an inclusive, collegial, and highly collaborative faculty member environment, with far-reaching efforts in multidisciplinary challenges. A sample of EECS faculty research activities can be found here .   The department is proud of its high-quality education programs and its nearly 100% placement rate in the industry or academic institutions. It possesses outstanding research resources such as laboratories in the John Mica Engineering and Aerospace Innovation Complex , and recent student support grants such as the National Science Foundation (NSF) CyberCorps® Scholarships for Service (SFS) , the NSF Scholarships in STEM (S-STEM), and two NSF Research Experiences for Undergraduates (REU) programs .   EECS seeks candidates who can expand the department’s research expertise, as well as deliver student-centered teaching and provide mentoring to undergraduate and graduate students. Applicants should share the department’s commitment to an inclusive, inviting and collaborative community. About us For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.   Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.   Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle! Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26. Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period. Qualifications Required Qualifications Candidates must hold a terminal degree in Systems Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Software Engineering, or a closely related field.   Applicants should demonstrate the potential for or record of scholarly achievement appropriate to the rank sought, as well as the ability to provide excellent instruction and mentoring to undergraduate and graduate students. Candidates should also demonstrate an ability to contribute to an inclusive, inviting, and collaborative academic community.   Priority consideration will be given to candidates whose research can contribute to the Center for Aerospace Resilient Systems , one of the University’s established Centers of Excellence. Additional consideration will be given to candidates with expertise in Model-Based Systems Engineering, digital twins, applications of systems engineering in aerospace fields, and human-subject experimentation. Excellent candidates in all areas of Systems Engineering will be considered.   Application process/requirements The anticipated start date is Spring 2027. Review of applications will begin upon receipt and continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, applications should be submitted by December 15, 2026.   To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R312103 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: Cover letter Full CV Statements of teaching philosophy Research plan Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)   Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.   Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website .   Embry-Riddle does not accept unsolicited assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. Agencies interested in partnering with the University should contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not contact hiring managers or other University employees directly.   To preserve the integrity and authenticity of our hiring process, candidates are expected to participate without AI-assisted coaching, real-time response generation, or recording during interviews or assessments. Embry-Riddle does not use AI to automatically screen, rank, or select candidates."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Administrative-Specialist_R312306": {
      "title": "Administrative Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-15\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity    Are you a highly organized professional who thrives on creating exceptional experiences, keeping operations running smoothly, and supporting executive-level initiatives? We are seeking an Administrative Specialist who brings professionalism, initiative, problem-solving, discretion, and a service-oriented mindset to a dynamic, collaborative and highly visible office environment.  This role offers a unique opportunity to coordinate executive events, collaborate with senior leaders, support special projects, and help deliver memorable experiences for distinguished guests, trustees, campus leaders, and community partners. The successful candidate will be a trusted team member who can manage multiple priorities, anticipate needs, and maintain a calm, polished presence while handling confidential and sensitive information.    Key Responsibilities Executive Events & Special Projects  Help plan and coordinate executive events, VIP visits, special engagements, and other high-profile initiatives.  Partner closely with the Sr. Executive Assistant to the President and other executive support staff to ensure seamless event logistics, including guest communications, transportation arrangements, catering coordination, event materials, and day-of flawless execution.  Track projects and event details with exceptional organization, attention to detail and follow-through.  Assist with annual signature initiatives, special mailings, gift programs, and other executive outreach efforts.  Utilize and support student assistants to ensure event preparation and execution is seamless.  Executive & Board Support  Collaborate with executive leadership support staff to coordinate meetings, programs, and events.  Provide operational support for biannual board meetings, retreats, and related activities, including preparation of materials, research, purchasing, tracking projects, and administrative coordination.  Contribute creative ideas and solutions that enhance efficiency and elevate the overall experience for participants.  Office Operations & Visitor Experience  Maintain a welcoming, professional office environment for visitors, guests, and campus partners.  Coordinate office supplies, inventory, equipment, mail services, deliveries, and general office organization.  Answer and direct inquiries with professionalism, courtesy, discretion and respect.  Maintain office displays, records, and organizational systems.  Support continuous improvement efforts that strengthen office processes and service delivery.  Team Collaboration  Work collaboratively across multiple departments and stakeholder groups to achieve outstanding results.  Provide backup support for key administrative functions as needed.  Build strong working relationships while maintaining the highest level of professionalism and discretion.  What We're Looking For  Strong organizational, project management, and event coordination skills.  Exceptional attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously.  Sound judgment, initiative, discretion, and professionalism.  Excellent interpersonal and customer service skills.  Ability to communicate effectively with a variety of audiences, including senior leaders, trustees, visitors, students, and community partners.  Strong technology skills, including Microsoft Office applications and other business productivity tools.  A collaborative, solutions-oriented approach with a focus on continuous improvement.  Ability to handle confidential and sensitive information with care.     About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.     Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.     Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.       Generous Time Off: Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave: Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.       Compensation     The hourly range for this role is up to $22.55. The final offer will be based on the candidate’s skills, qualifications, and experience, as well as applicable state regulations, internal equity, and business needs, and may fall outside of the stated range.  Qualifications Preferred Qualifications  Bachelor's degree.  One to three years of administrative, event planning, office management, or related experience.  Experience supporting executives, boards, leadership teams, or high-profile events is preferred.  Higher education experience is a plus.  Additional Information  Occasional work outside regular business hours will be required to support major events, including commencement activities and Board meetings. Overtime opportunities are typically available in conjunction with these events.  Must be eligible and willing to become an authorized campus vehicle driver.  This position is ideal for someone who enjoys bringing people together, managing meaningful projects from start to finish, and serving as a trusted administrative partner in a professional, mission-driven environment. Based on the position description and supplemental requirements provided.     To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R312306. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:  Cover letter  Resume  Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)     Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.     Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website .     Embry-Riddle does not accept unsolicited assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. Agencies interested in partnering with the University should contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not contact hiring managers or other University employees directly.   To preserve the integrity and authenticity of our hiring process, candidates are expected to participate without AI-assisted coaching, real-time response generation, or recording during interviews or assessments. Embry-Riddle does not use AI to automatically screen, rank, or select candidates."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Remote---United-States/Sponsored-Research-Contract-Administrator_R310831-1": {
      "title": "Sponsored Research Contract Administrator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-15\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity:    In this position, the Sponsored Research Contract Administrator will manage pre and post award activities for an assigned portfolio of contracts within the Office of Sponsored Research unit using knowledge of contract management rules and regulations, financial budget management, technical expertise, and analytical skills, including guidance on what issues may present a compliance liability to the university. Serve as a liaison among university administration, principal investigators, faculty, staff, and funding agency representatives. Responsible for providing guidance to principal investigators regarding federal and non-federal contract administration, including but not limited to adherence to FAR, DFAR, Part 2 CFR 200 of the Uniform Guidance and other government regulations including applicable policies, procedures, rules and regulations of the university and sponsoring agency. Responsible for monitoring and reporting on budget management of contracts awarded to the university. Responsible for recording and maintaining sponsored projects information in the university systems.  This position is eligible for hybrid/remote work.    About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.     Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.     Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.       Generous Time Off: Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave: Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.       Compensation     The annual salary range for this role is up to $62,000. The final offer will be based on the candidate’s skills, qualifications, and experience, as well as applicable state regulations, internal equity, and business needs, and may fall outside of the stated range.  Qualifications Required Education and Qualifications:  Bachelor's degree in business or related field with 3-5 years of related experience. CRA and/or Contract Certification(s) and master’s degree a plus. In lieu of a bachelor’s degree, 5-10 years of experience in contracts, grants, or financial management will be considered. Experience with sponsors who support aeronautical research (FAA, DoD, USAF, USSF, NASA etc.) a plus. Excellent attention to detail, outstanding customer service and strong communication skills are required for this position. Pre-award Contract management experience or demonstrated experience with managing multi-part contract proposals, technical documents, and budgets. Post-award Contract management experience or demonstrated experience with managing multi-part contracts, technical documents, and budgets. The ability to manage a high volume of work and competing deadlines in a fast-paced, deadline-driven work environment. Comfort working remotely and using tools to facilitate remote work, e.g., Teams, Zoom. Comfort with business systems that hold financial and administrative information, such as Workday. Proficiency with Microsoft 365, to include Microsoft Word, Shared Drives, OneDrive, and Excel, to include use and understanding of Excel formulas. Effective analytical and problem-solving skills. Preferred Qualifications: Familiarity with contracting guidelines as detailed in the FAR, DFAR, ITAR and CFR, also experience with STTR and SBIR contracts is a plus. Experience working in higher education with knowledge of Sponsored Research, including the principles, methods, and procedures of contract administration and compliance. Application process/requirements  To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the  Embry-Riddle Career Site  and search for requisition number R310831. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:  Cover letter  Full Resume  Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)     Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.     Embry-Riddle does not accept unsolicited assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. Agencies interested in partnering with the University should contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not contact hiring managers or other University employees directly. To preserve the integrity and authenticity of our hiring process, candidates are expected to participate without AI-assisted coaching, real-time response generation, or recording during interviews or assessments. Embry-Riddle does not use AI to automatically screen, rank, or select candidates."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Assistant-Director--Manager---Employer-Engagement-and-Signature-Events_R312315": {
      "title": "Assistant Director (Manager), Employer Engagement and Signature Events",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-15\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity    The Assistant Director (Manager), Employer Engagement and Signature Events plays a key role in advancing the strategic priorities of the Center for Career and Professional Development (CCPD) through the planning, coordination, marketing, and execution of employer engagement initiatives, signature recruiting events, and career expos. Working closely with the Executive Director, they support the development and maintenance of strong relationships with Eagle Career Champion Partners (ECCP) and other strategic employers. The position coordinates employer visits, recruiting activities, and engagement opportunities that connect students with industry professionals and expand access to internships, cooperative education, and full-time employment. The Manager is responsible for the operational planning and execution of major employer engagement initiatives, including Boeing Week, and serves as a primary coordinator for employer scheduling, communications, event logistics, and marketing. The position leads the planning and execution of the Daytona Beach Career Expo and collaborates with CCPD colleagues to support Career Expos and employer engagement activities at the Prescott and Worldwide campuses. The Manager works collaboratively with academic colleges, faculty, student organizations, and university departments to ensure coordinated employer engagement and exceptional service to students and industry partners. Additional responsibilities include overseeing the Student Ambassador Program, supporting assessment and reporting, and assisting the Executive Director with strategic initiatives. Primary Job Functions, Duties, and Accountabilities 1. Employer Engagement and Eagle Career Champion Partnerships Serve as a key point of contact for Eagle Career Champion Partners, coordinating employer engagement and recruiting opportunities throughout the academic year. Work directly with ECCP representatives to develop and maintain comprehensive schedules for campus visits, information sessions, classroom presentations, networking events, interviews, and student organization engagement. Coordinate with CCPD staff, academic colleges, faculty, and student organizations to maximize employer visibility and student participation. Maintain a comprehensive employer engagement calendar to ensure effective scheduling, communication, and coordination of campus resources. Support the Executive Director in maintaining and strengthening relationships with strategic industry partners, including Boeing, RTX, Gulfstream Aerospace, United Airlines, Honeywell, and other ECCP employers. Coordinate with Eagle Career Champion Partners to identify opportunities for engagement across the Daytona Beach, Prescott, and Worldwide campuses. Provide exceptional customer service and timely communication to employers before, during, and following campus visits. Track employer engagement activities, participation, and outcomes to support partnership development and continuous improvement. Collaborate with faculty, alumni, and student organizations to enhance employer engagement and visibility across the university. 2. Career Expos and Major Event Planning Lead the planning and execution of major Daytona Beach CCPD events, including the Career Expo, Soaring Together Networking Events, Interview Day, employer receptions, Resume Review Day, and industry-focused recruiting programs. Collaborate with CCPD leadership and staff at the Prescott and Worldwide campuses to support the planning and successful execution of their respective Career Expos and major employer engagement events. Assist Prescott and Worldwide colleagues with employer outreach, registration, marketing, communications, scheduling, and event logistics as needed. Coordinate with Eagle Career Champion Partners and other strategic employers to encourage participation in recruiting events across all three campuses. Oversee event logistics, including employer registration, venue reservations, space assignments, staffing, technology, signage, catering, and communications. Develop and maintain event planning timelines, operational procedures, and detailed schedules to ensure successful execution. Collaborate with campus partners to ensure events are inclusive, accessible, and aligned with student career development needs. Evaluate event outcomes through attendance reporting, employer feedback, student participation, and assessment tools. Identify opportunities to improve event operations, employer experiences, and student engagement. 3. Boeing Week and Signature Employer Engagement Programs Serve as the primary operational coordinator for Boeing Week and other large-scale, multi-day employer engagement initiatives. Develop and manage the Boeing Week master schedule in collaboration with Boeing representatives, the Executive Director, and CCPD staff. Coordinate classroom visits, engineering roundtables, student organization meetings, networking receptions, Boeing Scholars activities, veteran engagement events, presentations, and recruiting opportunities. Oversee logistics for employer representatives, including campus space reservations, event setup, audiovisual requirements, catering, transportation coordination, and visitor communications. Coordinate the Boeing Ambassador Program and student participation in Boeing Week activities. Collaborate with CCPD staff to ensure appropriate staffing, event coverage, and communication throughout the week. In partnership with the Associate Director develops promotional materials and communication plans to maximize student awareness and participation. In partnership with the Data Support Specialist maintains participation data, assess event outcomes, and prepares post-event summaries for the Executive Director and employer representatives. Apply successful Boeing Week practices to other signature employer engagement initiatives and strategic corporate partnerships. 4. Marketing, Communications, and Outreach Lead marketing and communication efforts across campuses promoting CCPD services, employer engagement activities, career expos, and recruiting opportunities. Assist with the development and coordination of marketing campaigns for Boeing Week, ECCP campus visits, employer information sessions, and other signature programs. Manage CCPD social media communications, including LinkedIn, Instagram, Facebook, and Handshake. Collaborate with university marketing and communications partners to ensure consistency in branding, messaging, and visual presentation. Develop promotional materials, employer announcements, student communications, digital signage, and event marketing content. Coordinate outreach to academic colleges, faculty, student organizations, and campus partners to increase student awareness and participation. Collaborate with Prescott and Worldwide CCPD staff to support coordinated marketing campaigns and employer communications for Career Expos and other recruiting initiatives. Maintain a comprehensive marketing calendar aligned with employer engagement and CCPD programming. Evaluate communication effectiveness and identify opportunities to improve student engagement and employer visibility. 5. Student Ambassador Program and Center Operations Provide leadership and oversight for the CCPD Student Ambassador Program. Recruit, train, schedule, supervise, and mentor student ambassadors supporting employer visits, career expos, and other Center initiatives. Coordinate ambassador assignments for Boeing Week, ECCP visits, and major recruiting events. Establish service expectations and ensure ambassadors provide a welcoming, professional experience for students and employers. Support daily CCPD operations and maintain high standards of customer service. Assist with program assessment, participation tracking, budget monitoring, and continuous improvement initiatives. Support special projects and strategic priorities as assigned by the Executive Director. About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.     Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.     Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.       Generous Time Off: Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave: Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications Required Qualifications Education: Bachelor's degree in Higher Education, Business, Communications, Marketing, or a related field. Experience: Three to five years of progressively responsible experience in career services, employer relations, event management, marketing, higher education administration, or a related field. Required Skills, Knowledge, and Abilities: 3-5 years of experience with demonstrated experience managing complex projects, events, and multiple competing priorities. Excellent written and verbal communication, project management, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Demonstrated ability to build and maintain productive relationships with corporate partners, university leadership, faculty, staff, and students. Experience coordinating employer engagement activities, events, or recruitment programs. Experience developing marketing materials, communication campaigns, and event promotional strategies. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and familiarity with career services, event management, and reporting platforms. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to manage complex schedules and logistical arrangements. Demonstrated commitment to exceptional customer service and continuous improvement. Ability to work independently, exercise sound judgment, and collaborate effectively with diverse stakeholders. Ability to work flexible hours, including occasional evenings and weekends during major events. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Business Administration, Communications, or a related discipline. Experience working with corporate partners, employer-sponsored programs, and strategic industry relationships. Experience coordinating multi-day recruiting events or major employer engagement initiatives. Familiarity with aerospace, aviation, engineering, and STEM industries and recruitment trends. Experience using Handshake, Qualtrics, Excel, and social media management platforms. Experience supervising student employees and coordinating student ambassador programs. Familiarity with university advancement, employer development, and industry partnerships. Experience supporting programs or events across multiple university campuses.    To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R312315. Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:   Cover letter  Resume  Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)     Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.     Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website .     Embry-Riddle does not accept unsolicited assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. Agencies interested in partnering with the University should contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not contact hiring managers or other University employees directly.   To preserve the integrity and authenticity of our hiring process, candidates are expected to participate without AI-assisted coaching, real-time response generation, or recording during interviews or assessments. Embry-Riddle does not use AI to automatically screen, rank, or select candidates."
