    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Prescott-AZ/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Air-Traffic-Management--NTT---Prescott-Campus_R312130": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Air Traffic Management (NTT), Prescott Campus",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-13\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity The College of Aviation at Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University in Prescott, Arizona invites applications for a non-tenure track position in Applied Aviation Sciences Department starting in January 2027 at the Assistant/Associate Professor level in the field of air traffic management.   The department is interested in candidates serving as the primary instructor who can teach lecture courses focused on air traffic control procedures and techniques based on current standards and demands of the national airspace. Faculty candidates should be able to teach air traffic basics courses in a way that is coherent and understanding to students with little-to-no previous aviation knowledge. As part of their appointment, the selected candidate will mentor students.   Applicants should be able to demonstrate ability to teach and develop classroom and laboratory courses across all levels of undergraduate education in basics of understanding, and advanced skillsets in the industry. Successful faculty candidates will have a strong commitment to undergraduate education both in the classroom and through experiential learning opportunities. The department has a strong focus on hands-on educational methods and emphasizes practical skills students will need after graduation.   About the Department of Applied Aviation Science The Department of Applied Aviation Science offers three programs created specifically to meet the growing demands for trained aviation industry professionals. Bachelor of Science degrees within the Department of Applied Aviation Sciences include Applied Meteorology, Air Traffic Management, and Uncrewed Aircraft Systems, in addition to an Associate of Science in Air Traffic Management. Minors include Air Traffic Management, Applied Meteorology, Uncrewed Aircraft Systems, and Geographic Information Systems.   About the College of Aviation The College of Aviation provides the aviation professionals of tomorrow with the knowledge, skills, abilities, and judgment necessary to succeed in a global aviation community. The College is committed to preparing students to be leaders in the aviation and aerospace industry. Our graduates are recognized both nationally and internationally, which reflects the mission of the College to cultivate values-based professionals in a dynamic and global environment.   About us For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.   Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.   Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.   Perks Await You at Embry-Riddle! Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26. Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period. Qualifications Required Education and Qualifications: Masters Degree or Bachelors Degree with requisite industry experience. FAA Air Traffic Control Specialist Certification Excellent communication and mentoring skills, being willing to work one-on-one with air traffic program students. Ideally, the applicant holds a master's or bachelor's degree, but with extensive work experience in the field, the requirement of a degree may be omitted. Applicants should provide statements on their professional air traffic control background and the names and contact information of three professional references. The position will remain open until filled.   Application process/requirements Review of applications will begin on September 04, 2026, and will continue until the position is fill.   To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R312130 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include: Cover letter Full CV Statements of teaching philosophy Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)   Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.   Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website .   Embry-Riddle is not seeking assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. All agencies are directed to contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not reach out to hiring managers or staff."
    },
    "https://embryriddle.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Daytona-Beach-FL/Senior-Payroll-and-Benefits-Accountant_R312308-1": {
      "title": "Senior Payroll and Benefits Accountant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-13\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Opportunity    Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University is seeking a detail-oriented and analytical Senior Payroll and Benefits Accountant to serve as a key financial resource for payroll and employee benefits accounting. This position is responsible for overseeing complex accounting activities, ensuring the accuracy and integrity of financial records, and supporting compliance with applicable accounting standards, tax regulations, and University policies. The Senior Payroll and Benefits Accountant will play an important role in financial reporting, account reconciliations, audit preparation, internal controls, and the ongoing evaluation of payroll and benefits-related financial processes. Working collaboratively with Payroll Services, Human Resources, Finance, and other University stakeholders, this position will analyze financial data, investigate discrepancies, identify opportunities for process improvement, and provide recommendations that support sound financial decision-making. The ideal candidate brings extensive accounting experience, strong technical knowledge of payroll and employee benefits, and the ability to translate complex financial information into meaningful insights. This individual will help strengthen accounting practices, improve reporting accuracy and efficiency, and maintain reliable financial processes in a deadline-driven environment while safeguarding confidential employee and financial information. Key Responsibilitie s Payroll and Benefits Accounting: Oversee and analyze payroll and employee benefits accounting activities, ensuring transactions are accurately recorded, properly classified, and reflected in the appropriate financial accounts and reporting periods. Financial Reporting and Analysis: Prepare, review, and analyze financial reports, account balances, and supporting schedules related to payroll, employee benefits, and associated liabilities and expenses. Account Reconciliations: Lead complex reconciliations of payroll and benefits-related general ledger accounts, research discrepancies, identify root causes, and coordinate timely resolution. Compliance and Taxation: Support compliance with generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP), payroll tax requirements, retirement plan regulations, healthcare benefit requirements, and applicable University policies and procedures. Audit Coordination: Prepare documentation and schedules for internal and external audits, respond to audit inquiries, and assist with the development and implementation of corrective actions when needed. Internal Controls and Risk Management: Evaluate payroll and benefits accounting controls, identify potential risks or control gaps, and recommend improvements to strengthen accuracy, accountability, and compliance. Process Improvement and Automation: Identify opportunities to streamline accounting workflows, improve reconciliation processes, enhance reporting tools, and implement efficiencies through technology and automation. Data Analysis and Reporting Tools: Develop and maintain dashboards, financial models, and reporting tools that support accurate analysis, reconciliation, forecasting, and informed decision-making. Cross-Functional Collaboration: Partner with Payroll Services, Human Resources, Finance, and other University stakeholders to resolve complex accounting issues, improve data integrity, and maintain consistent financial practices. Systems and Technology: Utilize relevant financial and HR systems, including Workday where applicable, to analyze transactions, validate data, support reporting, and improve accounting processes. Project Leadership: Lead or support accounting initiatives, system enhancements, process reviews, and other projects related to payroll and employee benefits accounting. Confidentiality and Documentation: Maintain the confidentiality and security of sensitive employee, payroll, benefits, and financial information while ensuring records and supporting documentation are accurate and accessible for authorized review. Technical Guidance and Recommendations: Provide accounting expertise, communicate findings to relevant stakeholders, and recommend practical solutions to complex financial issues and operational challenges. About us     For over 100 years, Embry-Riddle has been the world's leading aviation and aerospace university, educating more than 30,000 students across residential campuses in Daytona Beach, Florida, and Prescott, Arizona, as well as through a global network of Worldwide locations and online programs. With more than 165,000 alumni around the world, our impact reaches every corner of the aerospace, aviation, defense and technology industries.     Today, our faculty, researchers and professional staff are advancing innovation across aviation, space, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, autonomous systems and next-generation engineering. Working alongside industry leaders, government agencies and innovators, they are solving real-world challenges and shaping the technologies that will define tomorrow.     Whether you are an educator, researcher, administrator, technologist or industry professional, your work at Embry-Riddle will contribute to something bigger than a job. Join a community driven by discovery, purpose and excellence—and help shape the future of aerospace.       Generous Time Off: Enjoy up to 18 days of paid leave in your first year, including 3 days granted upon hire and 15 days accrued throughout the year. You'll also receive 9+ paid holidays, including the day after Thanksgiving and the week between Christmas Eve and New Year's Day.   Tuition Coverage: Get 100% tuition coverage for yourself for one undergraduate and one graduate degree, and discounted rates for your spouse and dependent children up to age 26.   Retirement Contributions: ERAU contributes 6% of your base salary to your retirement plan and offers a 4% matching contribution – with no vesting period.   Personal Leave: Relax with 15 days of personal leave for non-exempt employees or 18 days for exempt full-time employees in your first year.    Qualifications   Qualifications Education: Bachelor's degree or an equivalent combination of education and relevant work experience. Area of Concentration: Accounting, finance, tax, business administration, or a related field. Preferred Education: Master's degree in accounting, finance, business administration, or a related discipline. Experience: Seven years of progressively responsible experience in accounting, payroll accounting, benefits accounting, financial reporting, auditing, finance, or a related field. Required Skills and Knowledge : Advanced knowledge of payroll and benefits accounting, financial reporting, and GAAP. Expertise in internal controls, payroll taxation, retirement plans, healthcare benefits, and regulatory compliance. Experience leading or supporting internal and external audits. Ability to analyze complex financial data and provide strategic recommendations. Strong project management, process improvement, and problem-solving skills. Workday experience strongly preferred, including Payroll, Benefits, and Financials modules. Advanced Microsoft Excel skills, including pivot tables, complex formulas, data analysis, and financial modeling. Experience developing dashboards, reporting tools, and automated reconciliation processes. Strong communication, organizational, and cross-functional leadership skills. Ability to maintain confidentiality, manage competing priorities, and work independently in a deadline-driven environment. To submit your application for this opportunity, please visit the Embry-Riddle Career Site and search for requisition number R312308 . Please attach all relevant materials to your application when you apply online. Complete submissions include:  Cover letter  Resume  Contact information for at least three professional references (please note that references may be contacted as part of the interview/screening process)     Current Embry-Riddle employees: Please apply directly through the ERAU Employee Hub Central application within Workday.     Embry-Riddle is committed to fostering a workplace where all individuals are valued and respected. We strive to ensure that all faculty, staff, and students are treated fairly and provided equal opportunities for employment, advancement, compensation, training, and other benefits of employment. Embry-Riddle makes employment decisions — including hiring, promotions, compensation, and other terms of employment — based on individual merit, qualifications, and abilities. Embry-Riddle is strongly opposed to discrimination and harassment, and such behavior is prohibited by university policy. Embry-Riddle does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, veteran status, predisposing genetic characteristics, age, religion, or pregnancy status, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local law, in its employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, or other school-administered programs or activities. For further information, please visit our website .     Embry-Riddle does not accept unsolicited assistance from staffing or recruitment agencies. Agencies interested in partnering with the University should contact eraujobs@erau.edu and should not contact hiring managers or other University employees directly.   To preserve the integrity and authenticity of our hiring process, candidates are expected to participate without AI-assisted coaching, real-time response generation, or recording during interviews or assessments. Embry-Riddle does not use AI to automatically screen, rank, or select candidates."
    }
